VBI({"EVT-02600":{"k":"event","n":"Daniel hears how long until the end of the wonders","d":"One of two standing on the riverbanks asks how long until the end of the wonders, the man clothed in linen swears by Him who lives forever, and Daniel is told to go his way till the end (Daniel 12:5–13)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Daniel 12:7","v":"It would be for a time, times and half a time, and when the power of the holy people had been completely shattered, all these things would be finished"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Daniel 12:9–10","v":"The words are closed up and sealed till the time of the end; many would be purified, made white and refined, but the wicked would do wickedly and none of them understand, while the wise would understand"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Daniel 12:11–12","v":"From the time the daily sacrifice is taken away and the abomination of desolation is set up there would be one thousand two hundred and ninety days; blessed is he who waits and comes to the one thousand three hundred and thirty-five days"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Daniel 12:13","v":"Daniel would go his way till the end, rest, and arise to his inheritance at the end of the days"},{"p":"part of","r":"Daniel 12:5–13","e":"EVT-02593","q":5},{"p":"participant","r":"Daniel 12:5–13","e":"PER-02957"},{"p":"participant","r":"Daniel 12:5–13","e":"SPR-00016"},{"p":"participant","r":"Daniel 12:5–13","e":"GRP-01014"},{"p":"told in","r":"Daniel 12:5–13","v":"Daniel 12:5–13"}],"nm":{"EVT-02593":"Daniel's vision by the Tigris","GRP-01014":"The two on the riverbanks in Daniel's vision","PER-02957":"Daniel","SPR-00016":"The man clothed in linen in Daniel's vision"}},"EVT-02601":{"k":"event","n":"The prophecies of Hosea","d":"The word of the LORD to Hosea the son of Beeri, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and of Jeroboam the son of Joash, king of Israel (Hosea 1:1)","f":[{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:1–2","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:1–2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 1:1","v":"Hosea 1:1"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02602","EVT-02607","EVT-02608","EVT-02609","EVT-02610","EVT-02611","EVT-02612","EVT-02613","EVT-02614","EVT-02615","EVT-02616","EVT-02617","EVT-02619","EVT-02620","EVT-02621","EVT-02622"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02602":"Hosea's sign of his wife and children","EVT-02607":"The LORD's charge against Israel, His unfaithful wife","EVT-02608":"The LORD promises to betroth Israel to Himself forever","EVT-02609":"Hosea loves and buys an adulterous woman","EVT-02610":"The LORD's charge against the inhabitants of the land","EVT-02611":"The LORD's judgment on the priests, the house of Israel and the house of the king","EVT-02612":"The call to return to the LORD","EVT-02613":"The LORD's lament over the faithfulness of Ephraim and Judah","EVT-02614":"The LORD's word on the wickedness of Ephraim and Samaria","EVT-02615":"The LORD's word against Israel's kings, idols and altars","EVT-02616":"The LORD's word on Israel's days of punishment","EVT-02617":"The LORD's word on Israel's divided heart and the calf of Beth Aven","EVT-02619":"The LORD's love for Israel, His son","EVT-02620":"The LORD's charge against Judah and Jacob","EVT-02621":"The LORD's judgment on Ephraim and Samaria","EVT-02622":"The LORD's promise to heal Israel's backsliding","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02602":{"k":"event","n":"Hosea's sign of his wife and children","d":"At the LORD's word Hosea takes a wife of harlotry, Gomer the daughter of Diblaim, and the LORD names her children Jezreel, Lo-Ruhamah and Lo-Ammi as signs against the house of Jehu and the house of Israel, and foretells Israel's restoration (Hosea 1:2–2:1)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 1:2; Hosea 1:2","v":"Hosea was to take a wife of harlotry and children of harlotry, for the land had committed great harlotry (spiritual adultery, by the NKJV note) by departing from the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 1:4","v":"In a little while the LORD would avenge the bloodshed of Jezreel on the house of Jehu and bring an end to the kingdom of the house of Israel"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 1:5","v":"In that day He would break the bow of Israel in the Valley of Jezreel"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 1:6; Hosea 1:6","v":"He would no longer have mercy on the house of Israel, but would utterly take them away (or, by the NKJV note, that He might forgive them at all)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 1:7","v":"He would have mercy on the house of Judah and save them by the LORD their God, not by bow, sword or battle, horses or horsemen"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 1:9","v":"Israel was not His people, and He would not be their God"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 1:10; Hosea 1:10; Romans 9:26; 1 Peter 2:10","v":"Yet the children of Israel would be as countless as the sand of the sea, and where it was said to them that they were not His people (lo-ammi, by the NKJV note) they would be called the sons of the living God, words Paul quotes and Peter takes up"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:1; Hosea 1:11–2:1","v":"The children of Judah and of Israel would be gathered together, appoint one head and come up out of the land, for the day of Jezreel would be great; they would call their brethren 'My people' and their sisters 'Mercy is shown' (Ammi and Ruhamah, by the NKJV notes)"},{"p":"occurred before","r":"Hosea 1:2–3; 3:1","e":"EVT-02609"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 1:2–9","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:2–9","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:2–2:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:3–8","e":"PER-02970"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 1:2–2:1","v":"Hosea 1:2–2:1"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02603","EVT-02604","EVT-02605","EVT-02606"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","EVT-02603":"Hosea takes Gomer as his wife","EVT-02604":"Birth of Jezreel the son of Hosea","EVT-02605":"Birth of Lo-Ruhamah","EVT-02606":"Birth of Lo-Ammi","EVT-02609":"Hosea loves and buys an adulterous woman","PER-02968":"Hosea","PER-02970":"Gomer"}},"EVT-02603":{"k":"event","n":"Hosea takes Gomer as his wife","d":"At the LORD's word Hosea takes Gomer the daughter of Diblaim, a wife of harlotry (Hosea 1:2–3)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"2 Kings 14:29; 15:1, 8; Hosea 1:1–3","e":"EVT-01764","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"The LORD began to speak by Hosea when He told him to take a wife of harlotry, and Hosea went and took Gomer (Hosea 1:2–3). The word of the LORD came to Hosea in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz and Hezekiah and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash, and no earlier king is named (1:1): so it began no earlier than Uzziah's reign, which began in Jeroboam's twenty-seventh year (2 Kings 15:1), and no later than Jeroboam's death, which came before Zechariah his son reigned in Uzziah's thirty-eighth year (14:29; 15:8)."},{"p":"part of","r":"2 Kings 14:29; 15:1, 8; Hosea 1:1–3","e":"EVT-01768","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"The LORD began to speak by Hosea when He told him to take a wife of harlotry, and Hosea went and took Gomer (Hosea 1:2–3). The word of the LORD came to Hosea in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz and Hezekiah and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash, and no earlier king is named (1:1): so it began no earlier than Uzziah's reign, which began in Jeroboam's twenty-seventh year (2 Kings 15:1), and no later than Jeroboam's death, which came before Zechariah his son reigned in Uzziah's thirty-eighth year (14:29; 15:8)."},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 1:2–3","e":"EVT-02602","q":1},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:3","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:3","e":"PER-02970"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 1:2–3","v":"Hosea 1:2–3"}],"nm":{"EVT-01764":"The reign of Jeroboam the son of Joash","EVT-01768":"The reign of Azariah","EVT-02602":"Hosea's sign of his wife and children","PER-02968":"Hosea","PER-02970":"Gomer"}},"EVT-02604":{"k":"event","n":"Birth of Jezreel the son of Hosea","d":"Gomer bears Hosea a son, whom the LORD tells him to name Jezreel (Hosea 1:3–4)","f":[{"p":"birth of","r":"Hosea 1:3","e":"PER-02972"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 1:3–4","e":"EVT-02602","q":2},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:3","e":"PER-02970"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:3–4","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 1:3–4","v":"Hosea 1:3–4"}],"nm":{"EVT-02602":"Hosea's sign of his wife and children","PER-02968":"Hosea","PER-02970":"Gomer","PER-02972":"Jezreel"}},"EVT-02605":{"k":"event","n":"Birth of Lo-Ruhamah","d":"Gomer bears a daughter, whom God tells Hosea to name Lo-Ruhamah (Hosea 1:6)","f":[{"p":"birth of","r":"Hosea 1:6","e":"PER-02973"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 1:6","e":"EVT-02602","q":3},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:6","e":"PER-02970"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:6","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 1:6","v":"Hosea 1:6"}],"nm":{"EVT-02602":"Hosea's sign of his wife and children","PER-02968":"Hosea","PER-02970":"Gomer","PER-02973":"Lo-Ruhamah"}},"EVT-02606":{"k":"event","n":"Birth of Lo-Ammi","d":"When she has weaned Lo-Ruhamah, Gomer bears a son, whom God names Lo-Ammi (Hosea 1:8–9)","f":[{"p":"birth of","r":"Hosea 1:8","e":"PER-02974"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 1:8–9","e":"EVT-02602","q":4},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 1:8","e":"PER-02970"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 1:8–9","v":"Hosea 1:8–9"}],"nm":{"EVT-02602":"Hosea's sign of his wife and children","PER-02970":"Gomer","PER-02974":"Lo-Ammi"}},"EVT-02607":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's charge against Israel, His unfaithful wife","d":"The LORD bids Israel's children bring charges against their mother, who went after her lovers and the Baals, and says He will strip her and take back His gifts (Hosea 2:2–13)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:2; Hosea 2:2–4","v":"Unless she put away her harlotries and adulteries, He would strip her naked as on the day she was born, make her like a wilderness and a dry land and slay her with thirst; He would not have mercy on her children, for they were children of harlotry"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:6; Hosea 2:5–7","v":"Because she went after lovers she thought gave her bread and water, wool and linen, oil and drink, He would hedge up her way with thorns and wall her in (wall up her wall, by the NKJV note); she would chase her lovers and not find them, and then resolve to return to her first husband"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 2:8–10","v":"She did not know that He gave her grain, new wine and oil and multiplied her silver and gold, which they made ready for Baal; so He would take back His grain, new wine, wool and linen and uncover her lewdness before her lovers, and none would deliver her"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 2:11–13","v":"He would end her mirth, her feast days, New Moons, Sabbaths and appointed feasts, make the vines and fig trees she called her lovers' wages a forest for the beasts, and punish her for the days of the Baals, when she decked herself, went after her lovers and forgot Him"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 2:2–13","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 2:2–13","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 2:2–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 2:2–13","v":"Hosea 2:2–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02608":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises to betroth Israel to Himself forever","d":"The LORD will allure Israel into the wilderness, give her the Valley of Achor as a door of hope, take the names of the Baals from her mouth and betroth her to Himself forever (Hosea 2:14–23)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:14; Hosea 2:14–15","v":"He would allure her into the wilderness and speak comfort to her (to her heart, by the NKJV note), give her vineyards and the Valley of Achor as a door of hope, and she would sing there as in the days of her youth, when she came up from the land of Egypt"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:16; Hosea 2:16–17","v":"In that day she would call Him 'My Husband' and no longer 'My Master' (Ishi and Baali, by the NKJV notes), for He would take the names of the Baals from her mouth, and they would be remembered no more"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 2:18","v":"He would make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field, the birds and the creeping things, and shatter bow and sword from the earth, so that they would lie down safely"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 2:19–20","v":"He would betroth her to Himself forever in righteousness and justice, lovingkindness and mercy, and faithfulness, and she would know the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:22; Hosea 2:21–22","v":"In that day He would answer the heavens, they would answer the earth, the earth would answer with grain, new wine and oil, and they would answer Jezreel (God Will Sow, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 2:23; Hosea 2:23; Romans 9:25; 1 Peter 2:10","v":"He would sow her for Himself in the earth, have mercy on her who had not obtained mercy, and tell those who were not His people that they were His people, and they would call Him their God, words Paul quotes and Peter takes up"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 2:14–23","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 2:14–23","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 2:14–23","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 2:14–23","v":"Hosea 2:14–23"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02609":{"k":"event","n":"Hosea loves and buys an adulterous woman","d":"At the LORD's word Hosea loves a woman loved by a lover and committing adultery, buys her and bids her wait many days, a sign of Israel's many days without king or sacrifice and its return to the LORD (Hosea 3:1–5)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 3:1; Hosea 3:1","v":"Hosea was to go again and love a woman loved by a lover (friend or husband, by the NKJV note) and committing adultery, as the LORD loves the children of Israel, who look to other gods and love the raisin cakes of the pagans"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Hosea 3:3","v":"Hosea told the woman to stay with him many days, without playing the harlot or having a man, and he would be the same toward her"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 3:4","v":"The children of Israel would abide many days without king or prince, without sacrifice or sacred pillar, without ephod or teraphim"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 3:5","v":"Afterward they would return and seek the LORD their God and David their king, and fear the LORD and His goodness in the latter days"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 3:1–5","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 3:1–5","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 3:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 3:1–3","e":"PER-02975"},{"p":"price","r":"Hosea 3:2","v":"Fifteen shekels of silver and one and one-half homers of barley"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 3:1–5","v":"Hosea 3:1–5"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea","PER-02975":"The woman Hosea bought"}},"EVT-02610":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's charge against the inhabitants of the land","d":"The LORD charges Israel with having no truth, mercy or knowledge of God, with crime and with idols, and warns Judah not to offend as Israel does (Hosea 4:1–19)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Hosea 4:15","v":"Though Israel played the harlot, Judah was not to offend: not to come up to Gilgal or go up to Beth Aven, nor to swear by the life of the LORD there"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 4:3","v":"The land would mourn, and everyone who dwells in it would waste away, with the beasts, the birds and even the fish of the sea"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 4:5–6","v":"They would stumble by day and the prophet with them by night, and the LORD would destroy their mother; because they had rejected knowledge He would reject them as His priests, and because they had forgotten His law He would forget their children"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 4:7; NKJV notes, note on Hosea 4:9; Hosea 4:7–9","v":"The more they increased, the more they sinned, and He would change their glory into shame (by the NKJV notes, some traditions read 'They will change' and 'My glory'); it would be like people, like priest, and He would punish them for their ways and repay their deeds"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 4:10","v":"They would eat and not have enough, and commit harlotry and not increase, because they had ceased obeying the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 4:13–14","v":"The LORD would not punish their daughters and brides for harlotry and adultery, for the men themselves went apart with harlots, and a people without understanding would be trampled"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 4:16; Hosea 4:16–19","v":"Israel being as stubborn as a stubborn calf, the LORD would now let them forage like a lamb in open country (a large place, by the NKJV note); the wind had wrapped her up in its wings, and they would be ashamed of their sacrifices"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 4:1–19","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 4:1–19","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 4:1–19","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 4:1–19","v":"Hosea 4:1–19"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02611":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment on the priests, the house of Israel and the house of the king","d":"The LORD tells the priests, the house of Israel and the house of the king that the judgment is theirs, sounds the alarm over Ephraim and Judah, and says He will tear them like a lion and go back to His place till they seek Him (Hosea 5:1–15)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 5:1; Hosea 5:1","v":"The judgment was the priests', the house of Israel's and the king's house's (or, by the NKJV note, was for them), for they had been a snare at Mizpah and a net spread on Tabor"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 5:5–7","v":"Israel and Ephraim would stumble in their iniquity and Judah with them; they would go with their flocks and herds to seek the LORD and not find Him, for He had withdrawn Himself, and a New Moon would devour them and their heritage"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 5:8–10","v":"The ram's horn would sound in Gibeah and the trumpet in Ramah, and the cry go up at Beth Aven; Ephraim would be desolate in the day of rebuke, and the LORD would pour out His wrath like water on the princes of Judah"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 5:12–14","v":"He would be like a moth to Ephraim and like rottenness to the house of Judah, and like a lion and a young lion to them: He would tear them, take them away and go, and none would rescue"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 5:15; Hosea 5:15","v":"He would return to His place till they acknowledged their offense (became guilty or bore punishment, by the NKJV note), and then in their affliction they would earnestly seek His face"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 5:1–15","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 5:1–15","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 5:1–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 5:1–15","v":"Hosea 5:1–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02612":{"k":"event","n":"The call to return to the LORD","d":"Come, let us return to the LORD, who has torn and will heal, and who will revive after two days and raise up on the third day (Hosea 6:1–3)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 6:1; Hosea 6:1","v":"The LORD, who had torn and stricken, would heal them and bind them up (bandage, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 6:2","v":"After two days He would revive them, and on the third day raise them up, that they might live in His sight"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 6:3","v":"His going forth is established as the morning, and He would come to them like the rain, the latter and former rain on the earth"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 6:1–3","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 6:1–3","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 6:1–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 6:1–3","v":"Hosea 6:1–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02613":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's lament over the faithfulness of Ephraim and Judah","d":"The LORD asks what He shall do with Ephraim and Judah, whose faithfulness passes like a morning cloud, says He desires mercy and not sacrifice, and names their sins (Hosea 6:4–11)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 6:6; Hosea 6:6; Matthew 9:13; 12:7","v":"The LORD desires mercy (or faithfulness or loyalty, by the NKJV note) and not sacrifice, and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings, words Jesus bids His hearers learn"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 6:5; Hosea 6:5","v":"He had hewn them by the prophets and slain them by the words of His mouth, and His judgments (or the judgments on them, by the NKJV note) would be like light going forth"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 6:11","v":"A harvest was appointed for Judah, when the LORD would return the captives of His people"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 6:4–11","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 6:4–11","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 6:4–11","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 6:4–11","v":"Hosea 6:4–11"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02614":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word on the wickedness of Ephraim and Samaria","d":"When the LORD would heal Israel, the iniquity of Ephraim and the wickedness of Samaria are uncovered; their kings fall, and Ephraim, like a silly dove, calls to Egypt and goes to Assyria (Hosea 7:1–16)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 7:12","v":"Wherever they went the LORD would spread His net on them and bring them down like birds of the air, and chastise them as their congregation had heard"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 7:13","v":"Woe and destruction would come on them for fleeing from Him and transgressing against Him"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 7:16","v":"Their princes would fall by the sword for the cursings of their tongue, and this would be their derision in the land of Egypt"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 7:1–16","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 7:1–16","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 7:1–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 7:1–16","v":"Hosea 7:1–16"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02615":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against Israel's kings, idols and altars","d":"The trumpet sounds, for the enemy comes like an eagle: Israel has made kings and idols the LORD did not choose, the calf of Samaria will be broken, and they reap the whirlwind (Hosea 8:1–14)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 8:1; Hosea 8:1","v":"The trumpet (ram's horn, shophar, by the NKJV note) was to be set to the mouth"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 8:1–3","v":"One would come like an eagle against the house of the LORD, because they had transgressed His covenant and rebelled against His law; Israel had rejected the good, and the enemy would pursue him"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 8:5; Hosea 8:5–6","v":"The calf of Samaria was rejected (or had rejected them, by the NKJV note), and it would be broken to pieces, for a workman made it and it is not God"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 8:7–8","v":"They sow the wind and reap the whirlwind: the stalk has no bud and yields no meal, and if it did, aliens would swallow it up; Israel is swallowed up and is among the Gentiles like a vessel in which is no pleasure"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 8:10; Hosea 8:10","v":"Though they had hired among the nations, the LORD would gather them, and they would sorrow a little (or begin to diminish, by the NKJV note) because of the burden (or oracle, by the NKJV note) of the king of princes"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 8:13","v":"The LORD would remember their iniquity and punish their sins, and they would return to Egypt"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 8:14; Hosea 8:14","v":"He would send fire on Judah's cities, and it would devour his palaces (or citadels, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 8:1–14","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 8:1–14","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 8:1–14","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 8:1–14","v":"Hosea 8:1–14"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02616":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word on Israel's days of punishment","d":"Israel is not to rejoice, for the days of punishment have come: Ephraim will return to Egypt and Assyria, its glory will fly away, and they will be wanderers among the nations (Hosea 9:1–17)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:2","v":"The threshing floor and the winepress would not feed them, and the new wine would fail"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:3–5","v":"They would not dwell in the LORD's land: Ephraim would return to Egypt and eat unclean things in Assyria; they would offer no wine offerings to the LORD, and their bread would be like mourners' bread, not coming into His house"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:6","v":"Egypt would gather them up and Memphis bury them; nettles would possess their treasures of silver, and thorns be in their tents"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:7, 9","v":"The days of punishment and recompense had come, and Israel would know it; the LORD would remember their iniquity and punish their sins"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:11–14","v":"Ephraim's glory would fly away like a bird, with no birth, pregnancy or conception; the LORD would bereave them to the last man, and Ephraim would bring out his children to the murderer"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:15–16","v":"Because of the evil of their deeds the LORD would drive them from His house and love them no more; Ephraim was stricken, its root dried up, bearing no fruit"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 9:17","v":"God would cast them away because they did not obey Him, and they would be wanderers among the nations"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 9:1–17","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 9:1–17","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 9:1–17","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 9:1–17","v":"Hosea 9:1–17"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02617":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word on Israel's divided heart and the calf of Beth Aven","d":"Israel's altars grew with its fruit and its heart is divided: the calf of Beth Aven will be carried to Assyria, Samaria's king cut off and the high places of Aven destroyed (Hosea 10:1–15)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Hosea 10:12","v":"They were to sow righteousness, reap in mercy and break up their fallow ground, for it was time to seek the LORD till He came and rained righteousness on them"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 10:2–4","v":"The LORD would break down their altars and ruin their sacred pillars, and judgment would spring up like hemlock in the furrows of the field"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 10:5; Hosea 10:5–6","v":"The people of Samaria would fear and mourn for the calf of Beth Aven (calves, images, by the NKJV note), and its priests shriek for it, for its glory had departed; the idol would be carried to Assyria as a present for King Jareb, and Ephraim and Israel would be ashamed"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 10:7, 15","v":"As for Samaria, her king would be cut off like a twig on the water, and at dawn the king of Israel would be cut off utterly"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 10:8; Hosea 10:8; Luke 23:30; Revelation 6:16","v":"The high places of Aven (Idolatry or Wickedness, by the NKJV note), the sin of Israel, would be destroyed, thorn and thistle would grow on their altars, and they would say to the mountains 'Cover us!' and to the hills 'Fall on us!', words Jesus takes up"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 10:10; Hosea 10:10","v":"When the LORD desired, He would chasten them, and peoples would be gathered against them when He bound them for their two transgressions (or in their two habitations, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 10:11; Hosea 10:11","v":"Ephraim, a trained heifer that loves to thresh, would be harnessed to pull (ride, by the NKJV note) a plow; Judah would plow, and Jacob break his clods"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 10:14–15","v":"Tumult would arise among the people and all their fortresses be plundered, as Shalman plundered Beth Arbel; so it would be done to Bethel because of its great wickedness"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 10:1–15","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 10:1–15","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 10:1–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 10:1–15","v":"Hosea 10:1–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02618":{"k":"event","n":"Shalman plunders Beth Arbel","d":"In the day of battle Shalman plunders Beth Arbel, and a mother is dashed in pieces upon her children (Hosea 10:14)","f":[{"p":"occurred before","r":"Hosea 10:14","e":"EVT-02617"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 10:14","e":"PER-02976"},{"p":"place","r":"Hosea 10:14","e":"PLC-01431"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 10:14","v":"Hosea 10:14"}],"nm":{"EVT-02617":"The LORD's word on Israel's divided heart and the calf of Beth Aven","PER-02976":"Shalman","PLC-01431":"Beth Arbel"}},"EVT-02619":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's love for Israel, His son","d":"The LORD, who loved Israel as a child and called His son out of Egypt, cannot give Ephraim up, and will bring His sons back trembling from Egypt and Assyria (Hosea 11:1–12)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 11:5–6","v":"Israel would not return to the land of Egypt, but the Assyrian would be his king, because they refused to repent; the sword would slash in his cities and devour his districts"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 11:9; Hosea 11:8–9","v":"The LORD would not execute the fierceness of His anger nor destroy Ephraim again, nor come with terror (or enter a city, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 11:10–11","v":"They would walk after the LORD, who would roar like a lion, and His sons would come trembling from the west, like a bird from Egypt and a dove from the land of Assyria, and He would let them dwell in their houses"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 11:1–12","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 11:1–12","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 11:1–12","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 11:1–12","v":"Hosea 11:1–12"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02620":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's charge against Judah and Jacob","d":"The LORD brings a charge against Judah and will punish Jacob by his ways, recalling Jacob's struggle with the Angel and Ephraim's false scales (Hosea 12:1–14)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Hosea 12:6","v":"They were to return by the help of their God, keep mercy and justice, and wait on their God continually"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 12:2; Hosea 12:2","v":"The LORD brought a charge (a legal complaint, by the NKJV note) against Judah and would punish Jacob according to his ways and repay him by his deeds"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 12:9","v":"The LORD, their God ever since the land of Egypt, would again make them dwell in tents, as in the days of the appointed feast"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 12:11; Hosea 12:11","v":"Though Gilead had idols, which were vanity (worthless, by the NKJV note), and they sacrificed bulls in Gilgal, their altars would be heaps in the furrows of the field"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 12:14","v":"Because Ephraim provoked Him most bitterly, his Lord would leave the guilt of his bloodshed on him and return his reproach on him"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 12:1–14","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 12:1–14","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 12:1–14","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 12:1–14","v":"Hosea 12:1–14"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02621":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment on Ephraim and Samaria","d":"Ephraim, who died through Baal, will pass away like the morning cloud; the LORD will meet them like a lion and a bear, yet ransom them from the grave, and Samaria will fall by the sword (Hosea 13:1–16)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 13:3","v":"They would be like the morning cloud and the early dew that passes away, like chaff blown from a threshing floor and smoke from a chimney"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 13:8; Hosea 13:7–8","v":"The LORD would be to them like a lion, like a leopard lurking by the road and a bear robbed of her cubs, and would tear them open; the wild beast (beast of the field, by the NKJV note) would tear them"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 13:10; Hosea 13:9–11","v":"Israel was destroyed (it or he destroyed you, by the NKJV note), but its help was from the LORD, who would be its King (or who asks where its king is, in the Septuagint and other versions, by the NKJV note), while the king and princes they had asked for could not save them; He gave them a king in His anger and took him away in His wrath"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 13:12–13","v":"Ephraim's iniquity was bound up and his sin stored up; the sorrows of a woman in childbirth would come on him, an unwise son"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 13:14; Hosea 13:14; 1 Corinthians 15:55","v":"The LORD would ransom them from the power (hand, by the NKJV note) of the grave (or Sheol) and redeem them from death: O Death, He would be its plagues, O Grave its destruction (where is your sting, in the Septuagint, by the NKJV note), words Paul takes up"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 13:15","v":"An east wind, the wind of the LORD, would come up from the wilderness, dry up his spring and fountain, and plunder the treasury of every desirable thing"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 13:16; Hosea 13:16","v":"Samaria was held guilty (shall be disfigured, in the Septuagint, by the NKJV note), for she rebelled against her God: they would fall by the sword, their infants be dashed in pieces and their women with child ripped open"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 13:1–16","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 13:1–16","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 13:1–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 13:1–16","v":"Hosea 13:1–16"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02622":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's promise to heal Israel's backsliding","d":"Israel is called to return to the LORD with words of repentance, and the LORD promises to heal their backsliding and be like the dew to Israel (Hosea 14:1–9)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 14:2; Hosea 14:1–3; Hebrews 13:15","v":"Israel was to return to the LORD its God, taking words with it: to ask Him to take away all iniquity and receive them graciously, offering the sacrifices of their lips (bull calves; fruit, in the Septuagint, by the NKJV note), and to say that Assyria would not save them, that they would not ride on horses, nor call the work of their hands their gods, for in Him the fatherless finds mercy"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 14:4","v":"The LORD would heal their backsliding and love them freely, for His anger had turned away"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Hosea 14:5; Hosea 14:5–7","v":"He would be like the dew to Israel, who would grow (bud or sprout, by the NKJV note) like the lily and lengthen his roots like Lebanon, spread his branches, have the beauty of an olive tree and the fragrance of Lebanon; those under his shadow would return, revive like grain, grow like a vine, and be remembered like the wine of Lebanon"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Hosea 14:8","v":"Ephraim would say that he had nothing more to do with idols; the LORD, who heard and observed him, is like a green cypress tree, in whom his fruit is found"},{"p":"part of","r":"Hosea 14:1–9","e":"EVT-02601"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 14:1–9","e":"PER-02968"},{"p":"participant","r":"Hosea 14:1–9","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Hosea 14:1–9","v":"Hosea 14:1–9"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02601":"The prophecies of Hosea","PER-02968":"Hosea"}},"EVT-02623":{"k":"event","n":"The prophecies of Joel","d":"The word of the LORD to Joel the son of Pethuel: the locusts, the day of the LORD, the Spirit poured out and the judgment of the nations (Joel 1–3)","f":[{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 1:1","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 1:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 1–3","v":"Joel 1–3"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02625","EVT-02626","EVT-02627","EVT-02628","EVT-02629","EVT-02630"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02625":"The call to lament over the land laid waste","EVT-02626":"The LORD calls His people to return with all their heart","EVT-02627":"The LORD promises to restore the years the locusts have eaten","EVT-02628":"The LORD promises to pour out His Spirit on all flesh","EVT-02629":"The LORD's judgment of the nations in the Valley of Jehoshaphat","EVT-02630":"The LORD's blessing on Judah and Zion","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02624":{"k":"event","n":"Locusts and drought lay waste the land in Joel's day","d":"Swarm after swarm of locusts eats the land, the grain, new wine and oil fail, the brooks dry up and fire burns the pastures, so that the offerings are cut off from the house of the LORD (Joel 1:4–20; 2:25)","f":[{"p":"occurred before","r":"Joel 2:25","e":"EVT-02627"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:25","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"place","r":"Joel 1:9, 13–14; 2:1, 15–17; 3:1","e":"PLC-00945","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"Joel calls the priests of the house of the LORD to lament and the people to gather in Zion (Joel 1:9, 13–14; 2:1, 15–17), and the LORD's word is for Judah and Jerusalem (3:1)."},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 1:4–20; 2:25","v":"Joel 1:4–20; 2:25"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02627":"The LORD promises to restore the years the locusts have eaten","PLC-00945":"The kingdom of Judah"}},"EVT-02625":{"k":"event","n":"The call to lament over the land laid waste","d":"The elders, the drunkards, the farmers and the priests are called to lament, fast and cry out to the LORD, for the locusts and drought have laid the land waste and the day of the LORD is at hand (Joel 1:1–20)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Joel 1:2–3","v":"The elders and all the inhabitants of the land were to tell their children of it, and they their children, and they another generation"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Joel 1:5, 8, 11","v":"The drunkards were to wake and weep, the land to lament like a virgin in sackcloth for the husband of her youth, and the farmers and vinedressers to wail for the harvest"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Joel 1:13–14","v":"The priests were to put on sackcloth and lament, consecrate a fast, call a sacred assembly, gather the elders and all the people into the house of the LORD, and cry out to the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 1:15","v":"The day of the LORD was at hand, and it would come as destruction from the Almighty"},{"p":"part of","r":"Joel 1:1–20","e":"EVT-02623"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 1:1–20","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 1:1, 6–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 1:1–20","v":"Joel 1:1–20"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02623":"The prophecies of Joel","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02626":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD calls His people to return with all their heart","d":"The trumpet sounds in Zion for the day of the LORD and His great army, and the LORD calls His people to turn to Him with all their heart, with fasting and weeping (Joel 2:1–17)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:1; Joel 2:1","v":"The trumpet (ram's horn, by the NKJV note) was to be blown in Zion and the alarm sounded in the LORD's holy mountain, and all the inhabitants of the land were to tremble"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Joel 2:12–13","v":"The people were to turn to the LORD with all their heart, with fasting, weeping and mourning, and rend their heart and not their garments"},{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:17; Joel 2:15–17","v":"The trumpet was to sound in Zion for a fast and a sacred assembly: the people, the elders, the children and nursing babes, even the bridegroom and the bride, were to gather, and the priests to weep between the porch and the altar and ask the LORD to spare His people and not let the nations rule over (or speak a proverb against, by the NKJV note) His heritage"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 2:1–2","v":"The day of the LORD was coming, a day of darkness and gloom, of clouds and thick darkness, spreading like the dawn over the mountains"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:4; Joel 2:2–5","v":"A people great and strong would come, whose like had never been nor would be: fire before them and flame behind, the land like the garden of Eden before them and a desolate wilderness behind; they would look like horses and run like swift steeds (or horsemen, by the NKJV note), leap the mountains with the noise of chariots, and set themselves in battle array"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:8; Joel 2:6–9","v":"Peoples would writhe before them; they would run like mighty men and climb the wall like men of war, each keeping his column, unhalted by losses (by the NKJV note), running in the city and entering the windows like a thief"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 2:10–11","v":"The earth would quake and the heavens tremble, the sun and moon grow dark and the stars diminish their brightness; the LORD would give voice before His army, for the day of the LORD is great and very terrible, and none can endure it"},{"p":"part of","r":"Joel 2:1–17","e":"EVT-02623"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:1–17","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:1–17","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 2:1–17","v":"Joel 2:1–17"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02623":"The prophecies of Joel","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02627":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises to restore the years the locusts have eaten","d":"The LORD, zealous for His land, will send grain, new wine and oil, drive away the northern army, give the rain and restore the years the locusts have eaten (Joel 2:18–27)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 2:18–19","v":"The LORD would be zealous for His land and pity His people; He would send them grain, new wine and oil to satisfy them, and no longer make them a reproach among the nations"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:20; Joel 2:20","v":"He would remove the northern army far from them and drive him into a barren and desolate land, his face toward the eastern sea and his back toward the western sea, and his stench would rise because he had done monstrous (great, by the NKJV note) things"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:23; Joel 2:21–24","v":"The land and the beasts were not to fear, for the pastures would spring up and the fig tree and vine yield their strength; the children of Zion were to rejoice, for He had given them the former rain faithfully (or the teacher of righteousness, by the NKJV note) and would send the former and latter rain, and the threshing floors would be full of wheat and the vats overflow with new wine and oil"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:25; Joel 2:25–26","v":"He would restore the years that the swarming, crawling, consuming and chewing locusts had eaten, His great army which He sent among them; they would eat in plenty and praise His name, and His people would never be put to shame"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 2:27","v":"They would know that He is in the midst of Israel, the LORD their God and no other, and His people would never be put to shame"},{"p":"part of","r":"Joel 2:18–27","e":"EVT-02623"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:18–27","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:18–27","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 2:18–27","v":"Joel 2:18–27"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02623":"The prophecies of Joel","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02628":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises to pour out His Spirit on all flesh","d":"Afterward the LORD will pour out His Spirit on all flesh and show wonders in the heavens before the great day of the LORD, and whoever calls on His name will be saved (Joel 2:28–32)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 2:28–29; Acts 2:16–18","v":"Afterward the LORD would pour out His Spirit on all flesh: their sons and daughters would prophesy, their old men dream dreams and their young men see visions, and He would pour out His Spirit on menservants and maidservants in those days, words Peter quotes"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 2:30–31; Acts 2:19–20","v":"He would show wonders in the heavens and on the earth, blood and fire and pillars of smoke; the sun would be turned into darkness and the moon into blood before the great and awesome day of the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 2:32; Joel 2:32; Acts 2:21; Romans 10:13","v":"Whoever calls on the name of the LORD would be saved (or delivered, by the NKJV note), for in Mount Zion and in Jerusalem there would be deliverance (or salvation, by the NKJV note), as the LORD had said, among the remnant whom He calls, words Peter and Paul quote"},{"p":"part of","r":"Joel 2:28–32","e":"EVT-02623"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:28–32","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 2:28–32","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 2:28–32","v":"Joel 2:28–32"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02623":"The prophecies of Joel","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02629":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment of the nations in the Valley of Jehoshaphat","d":"The LORD will gather all nations into the Valley of Jehoshaphat and judge them for what they did to His people, and will roar from Zion as a shelter for His people (Joel 3:1–17)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 3:1–3","v":"When the LORD brought back the captives of Judah and Jerusalem, He would gather all nations into the Valley of Jehoshaphat and enter into judgment with them there for His people, His heritage Israel, whom they had scattered among the nations, for dividing up His land, and for casting lots for His people, giving a boy for a harlot and selling a girl for wine"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 3:4; Joel 3:4, 7–8","v":"If Tyre, Sidon and all the coasts of Philistia retaliated against Him (or repaid Him, by the NKJV note), He would swiftly return it on their own heads; He would raise His people from the place to which they had been sold, and sell their sons and daughters into the hand of the people of Judah, who would sell them to the Sabeans (Shebaites, by the NKJV note), a people far off"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 3:10; Joel 3:9–11","v":"The nations were to be told to prepare for war, rouse their mighty men, beat their plowshares into swords and their pruning hooks (pruning knives, by the NKJV note) into spears, let the weak say he is strong, and assemble and come"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 3:12–13; Revelation 14:15–19","v":"The nations would come up to the Valley of Jehoshaphat, where the LORD would sit to judge all the surrounding nations: the sickle was to be put in, for the harvest was ripe, the winepress full and their wickedness great, words John's vision repeats"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 3:14–15","v":"Multitudes would fill the valley of decision, for the day of the LORD is near there; the sun and moon would grow dark and the stars diminish their brightness"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 3:16–17","v":"The LORD would roar from Zion and utter His voice from Jerusalem, and heavens and earth would shake, but He would be a shelter for His people and the strength of the children of Israel; they would know that He is the LORD their God, dwelling in Zion His holy mountain, and Jerusalem would be holy, with no aliens passing through her again"},{"p":"part of","r":"Joel 3:1–17","e":"EVT-02623"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 3:1–17","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 3:1–17","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 3:1–17","v":"Joel 3:1–17"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02623":"The prophecies of Joel","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02630":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's blessing on Judah and Zion","d":"In that day the mountains will drip new wine, a fountain from the house of the LORD will water the Valley of Acacias, Egypt and Edom will be desolate, and Judah will abide forever (Joel 3:18–21)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Joel 3:18; Joel 3:18","v":"In that day the mountains would drip with new wine, the hills flow with milk and the brooks of Judah be flooded with water, and a fountain would flow from the house of the LORD and water the Valley of Acacias (Shittim, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 3:19","v":"Egypt would be a desolation and Edom a desolate wilderness, because of their violence against the people of Judah, for they shed innocent blood in their land"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Joel 3:20–21","v":"Judah would abide forever and Jerusalem from generation to generation, and the LORD would acquit them of the guilt of bloodshed He had not acquitted, for the LORD dwells in Zion"},{"p":"part of","r":"Joel 3:18–21","e":"EVT-02623"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 3:18–21","e":"PER-02977"},{"p":"participant","r":"Joel 3:18–21","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Joel 3:18–21","v":"Joel 3:18–21"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02623":"The prophecies of Joel","PER-02977":"Joel"}},"EVT-02631":{"k":"event","n":"The prophecies of Amos","d":"The words Amos saw concerning Israel in the days of Uzziah king of Judah and of Jeroboam the son of Joash, king of Israel, two years before the earthquake (Amos 1:1)","f":[{"p":"occurred before","r":"Amos 1:1","e":"EVT-02632"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 1:1","e":"EVT-01764"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 1:1","e":"EVT-01768"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 1:1","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 1:2–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 1:1","v":"Amos 1:1"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02633","EVT-02634","EVT-02635","EVT-02636","EVT-02637","EVT-02638","EVT-02639","EVT-02640","EVT-02641","EVT-02642","EVT-02643","EVT-02644","EVT-02645","EVT-02646","EVT-02647","EVT-02648","EVT-02649","EVT-02650","EVT-02651","EVT-02652","EVT-02653","EVT-02654"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-01764":"The reign of Jeroboam the son of Joash","EVT-01768":"The reign of Azariah","EVT-02632":"The earthquake in the days of Uzziah","EVT-02633":"The LORD's judgment on the nations for three transgressions and for four","EVT-02634":"The LORD's judgment on Judah for three transgressions and for four","EVT-02635":"The LORD's judgment on Israel for three transgressions and for four","EVT-02636":"The LORD will punish the family He has known","EVT-02637":"The LORD's word against Samaria and the altars of Bethel","EVT-02638":"The LORD's word to the cows of Bashan","EVT-02639":"The LORD calls Israel to prepare to meet its God","EVT-02640":"The lament for the virgin of Israel","EVT-02641":"The LORD calls the house of Israel to seek Him and live","EVT-02642":"The LORD's woe on those who desire the day of the LORD","EVT-02643":"The LORD hates Israel's feasts and will send it beyond Damascus","EVT-02644":"The LORD's woe on those at ease in Zion and Samaria","EVT-02645":"The LORD swears by Himself to deliver up the city","EVT-02646":"The LORD calls Amos from following the flock","EVT-02647":"The vision of the locusts","EVT-02648":"The vision of the fire","EVT-02649":"The vision of the plumb line","EVT-02650":"Amaziah the priest of Bethel opposes Amos","EVT-02651":"The vision of the basket of summer fruit","EVT-02652":"The LORD swears never to forget the deeds of those who swallow up the needy","EVT-02653":"The vision of the Lord standing by the altar","EVT-02654":"The LORD promises to raise up the tabernacle of David","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02632":{"k":"event","n":"The earthquake in the days of Uzziah","d":"An earthquake in the days of Uzziah king of Judah, from which the people fled, two years after Amos saw his words concerning Israel (Amos 1:1; Zechariah 14:5)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 1:1; Zechariah 14:5","e":"EVT-01768","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"Amos dates his words two years before the earthquake, in the days of Uzziah (Amos 1:1), and Zechariah speaks of the earthquake in the days of Uzziah king of Judah, from which the people fled (Zechariah 14:5)."},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 1:1; Zechariah 14:5","v":"Amos 1:1; Zechariah 14:5"},{"p":"years after","r":"Amos 1:1","v":"2 years","at":"EVT-02631"}],"nm":{"EVT-01768":"The reign of Azariah","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos"}},"EVT-02633":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment on the nations for three transgressions and for four","d":"For three transgressions and for four the LORD will not turn back the punishment of Damascus, Gaza, Tyre, Edom, the people of Ammon and Moab, but will send fire on their walls and palaces (Amos 1:2–2:3)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 1:5; Amos 1:4–5","v":"The LORD would send a fire into the house of Hazael to devour the palaces of Ben-Hadad, break the gate bar of Damascus, and cut off the inhabitant of the Valley of Aven and the one who holds the scepter (rules, by the NKJV note) in Beth Eden; the people of Syria would go captive to Kir"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 1:7–8","v":"He would send a fire on the wall of Gaza to devour its palaces, cut off the inhabitant of Ashdod and the one who holds the scepter in Ashkelon, and turn His hand against Ekron, and the remnant of the Philistines would perish"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 1:10","v":"He would send a fire on the wall of Tyre to devour its palaces"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 1:12","v":"He would send a fire on Teman to devour the palaces of Bozrah"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 1:14–15","v":"He would kindle a fire in the wall of Rabbah to devour its palaces amid shouting in the day of battle and a tempest in the day of the whirlwind, and the king of the people of Ammon would go into captivity with his princes"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 2:2–3","v":"He would send a fire on Moab to devour the palaces of Kerioth; Moab would die amid tumult, shouting and the sound of the trumpet, and He would cut off its judge and slay all its princes with him"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 1:2–2:3","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 1:2–2:3","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 1:2–2:3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 1:2–2:3","v":"Amos 1:2–2:3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02634":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment on Judah for three transgressions and for four","d":"For three transgressions of Judah and for four the LORD will not turn back its punishment, because they despised His law, and He will send fire on Judah and the palaces of Jerusalem (Amos 2:4–5)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 2:5","v":"He would send a fire on Judah to devour the palaces of Jerusalem"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 2:4–5","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 2:4–5","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 2:4–5","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 2:4–5","v":"Amos 2:4–5"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02635":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment on Israel for three transgressions and for four","d":"For three transgressions of Israel and for four the LORD will not turn back its punishment, for they oppress the poor and silence the prophets, though He brought them up from Egypt; in that day their mightiest will not escape (Amos 2:6–16)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 2:14; NKJV notes, note on Amos 2:15; Amos 2:14–16","v":"Flight would perish from the swift (or the place of refuge, by the NKJV note), the strong would not strengthen his power, and the mighty would not deliver himself; the archer would not stand, the swift of foot would not escape (or save himself, by the NKJV note), nor the horseman deliver himself, and the most courageous men of might would flee naked in that day"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 2:6–16","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 2:6–16","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 2:6–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 2:6–16","v":"Amos 2:6–16"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02636":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD will punish the family He has known","d":"The LORD tells the children of Israel, the whole family He brought up from Egypt, that He has known them only of all the families of the earth and so will punish them, and that He does nothing without revealing it to His servants the prophets (Amos 3:1–8)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 3:2","v":"Because He had known only them of all the families of the earth, He would punish them for all their iniquities"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 3:1–8","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 3:1–8","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 3:1–8","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 3:1–8","v":"Amos 3:1–8"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02637":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against Samaria and the altars of Bethel","d":"The LORD calls Ashdod and Egypt to see the tumults and oppression in Samaria, and foretells an adversary around the land, a remnant snatched like pieces from a lion's mouth, and destruction on the altars of Bethel and the great houses (Amos 3:9–15)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 3:9; Amos 3:9","v":"It was to be proclaimed in the palaces at Ashdod (Assyria in the Septuagint, by the NKJV note) and in the land of Egypt that they should gather on the mountains of Samaria and see the great tumults and the oppressed (or oppression) within her"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 3:13","v":"Those called were to hear and testify against the house of Jacob"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 3:11","v":"An adversary would be all around the land; he would sap their strength and their palaces would be plundered"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 3:12; Amos 3:12","v":"As a shepherd takes (or snatches, by the NKJV note) two legs or a piece of an ear from a lion's mouth, so the children of Israel who dwell in Samaria would be taken out, with a bed's corner and a couch's edge (the Hebrew uncertain, possibly the cover)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 3:14","v":"In the day He punished Israel for their transgressions, He would also bring destruction on the altars of Bethel, and the horns of the altar would be cut off and fall to the ground"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 3:15; Amos 3:15","v":"He would destroy (strike, by the NKJV note) the winter house along with the summer house; the houses of ivory would perish and the great houses come to an end"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 3:9–15","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 3:9–15","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 3:9–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 3:9–15","v":"Amos 3:9–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02638":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word to the cows of Bashan","d":"The LORD swears by His holiness that those on the mountain of Samaria whom He calls cows of Bashan, who oppress the poor, will be taken away with fishhooks through broken walls (Amos 4:1–3)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 4:3; Amos 4:2–3","v":"The Lord GOD swore by His holiness that the days would come when they would be taken away with fishhooks, and their posterity with fishhooks; they would go out through broken walls, each one straight ahead, and be cast (or cast them, by the NKJV note) into Harmon"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 4:1–3","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 4:1–3","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 4:1–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 4:1–3","v":"Amos 4:1–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02639":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD calls Israel to prepare to meet its God","d":"The LORD charges Israel with multiplying transgression at Bethel and Gilgal and with not returning to Him through hunger, drought, blight, plague, sword and overthrow, and bids it prepare to meet its God (Amos 4:4–13)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 4:12","v":"Because He would do this to them, Israel was to prepare to meet its God"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 4:4–13","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 4:4–13","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 4:4–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 4:4–13","v":"Amos 4:4–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02640":{"k":"event","n":"The lament for the virgin of Israel","d":"Amos takes up a lament for the house of Israel: the virgin of Israel has fallen to rise no more, and its cities will be left a tenth (Amos 5:1–3)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:2","v":"The virgin of Israel had fallen and would rise no more; she lay forsaken on her land, with no one to raise her up"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:3","v":"The city that went out by a thousand would have a hundred left, and the one that went out by a hundred would have ten left, to the house of Israel"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 5:1–3","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:1–3","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:1–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 5:1–3","v":"Amos 5:1–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02641":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD calls the house of Israel to seek Him and live","d":"The LORD bids the house of Israel seek Him and live, and not Bethel, Gilgal or Beersheba, to seek good and establish justice in the gate (Amos 5:4–15)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 5:4–6","v":"The house of Israel was to seek the LORD and live, and not seek Bethel, enter Gilgal or cross over to Beersheba"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 5:14–15","v":"They were to seek good and not evil, that they might live; to hate evil, love good and establish justice in the gate"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:5","v":"Gilgal would surely go into captivity, and Bethel would come to nothing"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:6","v":"Unless they sought the LORD, He would break out like fire in the house of Joseph and devour it, with no one to quench it in Bethel"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 5:11; Amos 5:11","v":"Though they had built houses of hewn stone they would not dwell in them, and though they had planted pleasant (desirable, by the NKJV note) vineyards they would not drink their wine"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:14–15","v":"Then the LORD God of hosts would be with them, as they had said, and it might be that He would be gracious to the remnant of Joseph"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 5:4–15","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:4–15","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:4–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 5:4–15","v":"Amos 5:4–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02642":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's woe on those who desire the day of the LORD","d":"There will be wailing in every street and vineyard when the LORD passes through, and the day of the LORD those who desire it will be darkness and not light (Amos 5:16–20)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:16–17","v":"There would be wailing in all the streets and highways; the farmer would be called to mourning and skillful mourners to wailing, and there would be wailing in all the vineyards, for the LORD would pass through them"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:18–20","v":"The day of the LORD would be darkness and not light for those who desired it, as when a man flees from a lion and a bear meets him, or leans his hand on the wall at home and a serpent bites him; very dark, with no brightness in it"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 5:16–20","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:16–20","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:16–20","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 5:16–20","v":"Amos 5:16–20"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02643":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD hates Israel's feasts and will send it beyond Damascus","d":"The LORD hates their feasts and offerings and bids justice run down like water; they carried Sikkuth and Chiun, and He will send them into captivity beyond Damascus (Amos 5:21–27)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 5:24","v":"Justice was to run down like water, and righteousness like a mighty stream"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 5:27; Acts 7:43","v":"He would send them into captivity beyond Damascus, words Stephen quotes as beyond Babylon"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 5:21–27","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:21–27","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 5:21–27","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 5:21–27","v":"Amos 5:21–27"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02644":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's woe on those at ease in Zion and Samaria","d":"Woe to the notable persons at ease in Zion and trusting in Mount Samaria, who lie on beds of ivory and drink wine from bowls but do not grieve for the affliction of Joseph: they will go captive first (Amos 6:1–7)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 6:2","v":"They were to go over to Calneh, Hamath the great and Gath of the Philistines, and see whether they were better than those kingdoms or their territory greater"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 6:7","v":"Therefore they would now go captive as the first of the captives, and those who recline at banquets would be removed"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 6:1–7","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 6:1–7","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 6:1–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 6:1–7","v":"Amos 6:1–7"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02645":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD swears by Himself to deliver up the city","d":"The Lord GOD swears by Himself that He abhors the pride of Jacob and will deliver up the city, and that He will raise up a nation to afflict Israel from the entrance of Hamath to the Valley of the Arabah (Amos 6:8–14)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 6:8","v":"The Lord GOD swore by Himself that He would deliver up the city and all that is in it"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 6:10; Amos 6:9–10","v":"If ten men remained in one house they would die; when a relative (his loved one or uncle, by the NKJV note) came with the one who would burn the bodies to carry them out, and asked whether any were left inside, he would be told none, and would bid silence, for they dare not mention the name of the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 6:11","v":"At the LORD's command the great house would be broken into bits and the little house into pieces"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 6:14","v":"The LORD God of hosts would raise up a nation against the house of Israel, and it would afflict them from the entrance of Hamath to the Valley of the Arabah"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 6:8–14","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 6:8–14","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 6:8–14","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 6:8–14","v":"Amos 6:8–14"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02646":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD calls Amos from following the flock","d":"The LORD takes Amos, a sheepbreeder and tender of sycamore fruit, from following the flock and sends him to prophesy to His people Israel (Amos 7:14–15)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Amos 7:15","v":"Amos was to go and prophesy to the LORD's people Israel"},{"p":"occurred before","r":"Amos 7:14–15","e":"EVT-02650"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 7:14–15","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:14–15","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:14–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 7:14–15","v":"Amos 7:14–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","EVT-02650":"Amaziah the priest of Bethel opposes Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02647":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of the locusts","d":"The Lord GOD shows Amos locust swarms formed at the late crop; when they have eaten the grass of the land Amos pleads that Jacob may stand, and the LORD relents (Amos 7:1–3)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 7:1–3","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:1–3","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:1–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 7:1–3","v":"Amos 7:1–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02648":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of the fire","d":"The Lord GOD shows Amos a judgment by fire that consumes the great deep and the land; Amos pleads again, and the LORD relents (Amos 7:4–6)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 7:4–6","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:4–6","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:4–6","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 7:4–6","v":"Amos 7:4–6"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02649":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of the plumb line","d":"The Lord stands on a wall with a plumb line in His hand and sets a plumb line among His people Israel: the high places of Isaac will be desolate, and He will rise with the sword against the house of Jeroboam (Amos 7:7–9)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 7:9; Amos 7:8–9","v":"He was setting a plumb line in the midst of His people Israel and would not pass by them anymore; the high places (places of pagan worship, by the NKJV note) of Isaac would be desolate and the sanctuaries of Israel laid waste, and He would rise with the sword against the house of Jeroboam"},{"p":"occurred before","r":"Amos 7:9–11","e":"EVT-02650","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"Amaziah's report that Amos said Jeroboam would die by the sword (Amos 7:10–11) follows the LORD's word that He would rise with the sword against the house of Jeroboam (7:9)."},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 7:7–9","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:7–9","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:7–9","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 7:7–9","v":"Amos 7:7–9"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","EVT-02650":"Amaziah the priest of Bethel opposes Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02650":{"k":"event","n":"Amaziah the priest of Bethel opposes Amos","d":"Amaziah the priest of Bethel reports Amos to Jeroboam as a conspirator and bids him flee to Judah; Amos answers that the LORD sent him, and foretells Amaziah's end and Israel's captivity (Amos 7:10–17)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 7:17","v":"The LORD said Amaziah's wife would be a harlot in the city, his sons and daughters would fall by the sword, his land would be divided by survey line, he would die in a defiled land, and Israel would surely be led away captive from its own land"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 7:10–17","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:10–17","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:15–17","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:10–17","e":"PER-02980"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 7:10–11","e":"PER-01081"},{"p":"place","r":"Amos 7:10, 13","e":"PLC-00006","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"Amaziah, the priest of Bethel, bids Amos prophesy no more at Bethel, the king's sanctuary (Amos 7:10, 13)."},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 7:10–17","v":"Amos 7:10–17"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-01081":"Jeroboam","PER-02979":"Amos","PER-02980":"Amaziah","PLC-00006":"Bethel"}},"EVT-02651":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of the basket of summer fruit","d":"The Lord GOD shows Amos a basket of summer fruit: the end has come on His people Israel, and the songs of the temple will be wailing (Amos 8:1–3)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 8:2–3","v":"The end had come upon His people Israel, and He would not pass by them anymore; the songs of the temple would be wailing in that day, with many dead bodies everywhere, thrown out in silence"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 8:1–3","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 8:1–3","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 8:1–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 8:1–3","v":"Amos 8:1–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02652":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD swears never to forget the deeds of those who swallow up the needy","d":"The LORD swears by the pride of Jacob against those who cheat and buy the poor: the sun will go down at noon, feasts will turn to mourning, and a famine of hearing His words will come (Amos 8:4–14)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 8:8; Amos 8:7–8","v":"The LORD swore by the pride of Jacob never to forget any of their works; the land would tremble and all who dwell in it mourn, and all of it would swell like the River (the Nile, by the NKJV note), heave and subside like the River of Egypt"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 8:9; Amos 8:9–10","v":"In that day He would make the sun go down at noon and darken the earth in broad daylight (a day of light, by the NKJV note), turn their feasts into mourning and their songs into lamentation, and bring sackcloth on every waist and baldness on every head, like mourning for an only son, its end a bitter day"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 8:11–13","v":"The days were coming when He would send a famine on the land, not of bread or water but of hearing the words of the LORD; they would wander from sea to sea and from north to east seeking the word of the LORD and not find it, and the fair virgins and strong young men would faint from thirst"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 8:14; Amos 8:14","v":"Those who swear by the sin of Samaria (or Ashima, a Syrian goddess, by the NKJV note), by the god of Dan and by the way of Beersheba would fall and never rise again"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 8:4–14","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 8:4–14","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 8:4–14","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 8:4–14","v":"Amos 8:4–14"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02653":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of the Lord standing by the altar","d":"Amos sees the Lord standing by the altar: none will escape His sword; He will destroy the sinful kingdom from the earth, yet not utterly destroy the house of Jacob, but sift the house of Israel among the nations (Amos 9:1–10)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 9:1; Amos 9:1","v":"The doorposts (capitals of the pillars, by the NKJV note) were to be struck so that the thresholds shook, and broken on the heads of them all"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 9:2; Amos 9:1–4","v":"He would slay the last of them with the sword, and none who fled would escape: though they dug into hell (or Sheol, by the NKJV note) or climbed to heaven, hid on top of Carmel or at the bottom of the sea, or went into captivity before their enemies, His hand, the serpent or the sword would find them, for He would set His eyes on them for harm and not for good"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 9:9; Amos 9:8–9","v":"The eyes of the Lord GOD were on the sinful kingdom, and He would destroy it from the face of the earth, yet not utterly destroy the house of Jacob; He would sift (shake, by the NKJV note) the house of Israel among all nations as grain is sifted in a sieve, yet not the smallest grain would fall to the ground"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 9:10","v":"All the sinners of His people who said calamity would not overtake them would die by the sword"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 9:1–10","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 9:1–10","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 9:1–10","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 9:1–10","v":"Amos 9:1–10"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02654":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises to raise up the tabernacle of David","d":"On that day the LORD will raise up the fallen tabernacle of David, bring back the captives of His people Israel and plant them in their land, never again to be pulled up (Amos 9:11–15)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Amos 9:11; NKJV notes, note on Amos 9:12; Amos 9:11–12; Acts 15:16–17","v":"On that day He would raise up the tabernacle (a booth, a figure of a deposed dynasty, by the NKJV note) of David that had fallen, wall up its breaches, raise its ruins and rebuild it as in the days of old, that they might possess the remnant of Edom and all the Gentiles (mankind in the Septuagint, by the NKJV note) called by His name, words James quotes"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 9:13","v":"The days were coming when the plowman would overtake the reaper and the treader of grapes the sower, and the mountains would drip with sweet wine and all the hills flow with it"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Amos 9:14–15","v":"He would bring back the captives of His people Israel; they would build the waste cities and live in them, plant vineyards and drink their wine, make gardens and eat their fruit; He would plant them in their land, and they would never again be pulled up from the land He had given them"},{"p":"part of","r":"Amos 9:11–15","e":"EVT-02631"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 9:11–15","e":"PER-02979"},{"p":"participant","r":"Amos 9:11–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Amos 9:11–15","v":"Amos 9:11–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02631":"The prophecies of Amos","PER-02979":"Amos"}},"EVT-02655":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of Obadiah","d":"The vision in which the Lord GOD speaks concerning Edom and foretells the kingdom that shall be His (Obadiah 1:1–21)","f":[{"p":"participant","r":"Obadiah 1:1","e":"PER-02981"},{"p":"participant","r":"Obadiah 1:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Obadiah 1:1–21","v":"Obadiah 1:1–21"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02656","EVT-02657"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02656":"The LORD's judgment on Edom for violence against his brother Jacob","EVT-02657":"The LORD's promise of deliverance on Mount Zion","PER-02981":"Obadiah"}},"EVT-02656":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's judgment on Edom for violence against his brother Jacob","d":"The Lord GOD will bring Edom down from the clefts of the rock, and for its violence against its brother Jacob on the day strangers cast lots for Jerusalem, shame will cover it, as the day of the LORD on all the nations draws near (Obadiah 1:1–16)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Obadiah 1:1","v":"A report had come from the LORD and a messenger had been sent among the nations, bidding them rise up against Edom for battle"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Obadiah 1:2–4","v":"The LORD would make Edom small among the nations and greatly despised; though it rose as high as the eagle and set its nest among the stars, He would bring it down"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Obadiah 1:7; Obadiah 1:5–7","v":"Thieves or grape-gatherers would have left something, but Esau would be searched out and his hidden treasures sought; the men of his confederacy would force him to the border, those at peace with him would deceive and prevail against him, and those who eat his bread would lay a trap (or wound or plot, by the NKJV note) for him, unperceived"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Obadiah 1:8–9","v":"In that day the LORD would destroy the wise men from Edom and understanding from the mountains of Esau, and the mighty men of Teman would be dismayed, so that everyone from the mountains of Esau would be cut off by slaughter"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Obadiah 1:10","v":"For violence against his brother Jacob, shame would cover Edom and it would be cut off forever"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Obadiah 1:15; Obadiah 1:15–16","v":"The day of the LORD upon all the nations was near: as Edom had done, it would be done to it, its reprisal (or reward, by the NKJV note) returning on its own head; as they drank on His holy mountain, so all the nations would drink continually and be as though they had never been"},{"p":"part of","r":"Obadiah 1:1–16","e":"EVT-02655"},{"p":"participant","r":"Obadiah 1:1–16","e":"PER-02981"},{"p":"participant","r":"Obadiah 1:1–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Obadiah 1:1–16","v":"Obadiah 1:1–16"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02655":"The vision of Obadiah","PER-02981":"Obadiah"}},"EVT-02657":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's promise of deliverance on Mount Zion","d":"On Mount Zion there will be deliverance, the house of Jacob will consume the house of Esau and possess the land, and the kingdom will be the LORD's (Obadiah 1:17–21)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Obadiah 1:17; Obadiah 1:17","v":"On Mount Zion there would be deliverance (or salvation, by the NKJV note) and holiness, and the house of Jacob would possess their possessions"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Obadiah 1:18","v":"The house of Jacob would be a fire and the house of Joseph a flame, and the house of Esau stubble for them to kindle and devour, so that no survivor of the house of Esau would remain, for the LORD had spoken"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Obadiah 1:19; Obadiah 1:19","v":"The South (the Negev, by the NKJV note) would possess the mountains of Esau and the Lowland Philistia; they would possess the fields of Ephraim and of Samaria, and Benjamin would possess Gilead"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Obadiah 1:20; Obadiah 1:20","v":"The captives of this host of the children of Israel would possess the land of the Canaanites as far as Zarephath, and the captives of Jerusalem who are in Sepharad would possess the cities of the South (the Negev, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Obadiah 1:21; Obadiah 1:21","v":"Saviors (deliverers, by the NKJV note) would come to Mount Zion to judge the mountains of Esau, and the kingdom would be the LORD's"},{"p":"part of","r":"Obadiah 1:17–21","e":"EVT-02655"},{"p":"participant","r":"Obadiah 1:17–21","e":"PER-02981"},{"p":"participant","r":"Obadiah 1:17–21","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Obadiah 1:17–21","v":"Obadiah 1:17–21"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02655":"The vision of Obadiah","PER-02981":"Obadiah"}},"EVT-02658":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","d":"The LORD sends Jonah the son of Amittai to cry out against Nineveh; Jonah flees toward Tarshish, is thrown into the sea and swallowed by a great fish, then preaches in Nineveh, which repents, and the LORD spares the city (Jonah 1–4)","f":[{"p":"destination","r":"Jonah 1:2; 3:2–3","e":"PLC-00038"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:1–3; 3:3","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:1–2; 3:1–2, 10","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 1–4","v":"Jonah 1–4"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02659","EVT-02660","EVT-02661","EVT-02662","EVT-02663","EVT-02664","EVT-02665","EVT-02666","EVT-02667","EVT-02668","EVT-02669","EVT-02670"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02659":"The LORD tells Jonah to cry out against Nineveh","EVT-02660":"Jonah flees toward Tarshish from the presence of the LORD","EVT-02661":"The LORD sends a great storm on Jonah's ship","EVT-02662":"A great fish swallows Jonah","EVT-02663":"Jonah prays from the fish's belly","EVT-02664":"The fish vomits Jonah onto dry land","EVT-02665":"The word of the LORD comes to Jonah a second time","EVT-02666":"Jonah cries out against Nineveh","EVT-02667":"The people of Nineveh repent","EVT-02668":"God relents from the disaster He said He would bring on Nineveh","EVT-02669":"Jonah is angry that the LORD spares Nineveh","EVT-02670":"The LORD prepares a plant, a worm and an east wind for Jonah","PER-01084":"Jonah","PLC-00038":"Nineveh"}},"EVT-02659":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD tells Jonah to cry out against Nineveh","d":"The word of the LORD comes to Jonah the son of Amittai to go to Nineveh, that great city, and cry out against it (Jonah 1:1–2)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Jonah 1:2","v":"Jonah was to arise and go to Nineveh, that great city, and cry out against it, for its wickedness had come up before the LORD"},{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 1:1–2","e":"EVT-02658","q":1},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:1","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:1–2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 1:1–2","v":"Jonah 1:1–2"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah"}},"EVT-02660":{"k":"event","n":"Jonah flees toward Tarshish from the presence of the LORD","d":"Jonah goes down to Joppa, finds a ship going to Tarshish, pays the fare and goes aboard, to flee from the presence of the LORD (Jonah 1:3)","f":[{"p":"destination","r":"Jonah 1:3","e":"PLC-01128"},{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 1:3","e":"EVT-02658","q":2},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:3","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"place","r":"Jonah 1:3","e":"PLC-00674"},{"p":"price","r":"Jonah 1:3","v":"The fare of a ship going to Tarshish"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 1:3","v":"Jonah 1:3"}],"nm":{"EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah","PLC-00674":"Joppa","PLC-01128":"Tarshish"}},"EVT-02661":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD sends a great storm on Jonah's ship","d":"The LORD sends a great wind on the sea; the lot falls on Jonah, and the mariners throw him into the sea, which grows calm, and they fear the LORD (Jonah 1:4–16)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 1:4–16","e":"EVT-02658","q":3},{"p":"participant","r":"NKJV notes, note on Jonah 1:4; Jonah 1:4, 14–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:5–15","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:6","e":"PER-02982"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:5–16","e":"GRP-01019"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 1:4–16","v":"Jonah 1:4–16"},{"p":"vow","r":"Jonah 1:16","v":"The mariners took vows to the LORD, with a sacrifice"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","GRP-01019":"The mariners of the ship Jonah took to Tarshish","PER-01084":"Jonah","PER-02982":"The captain of the ship Jonah took to Tarshish"}},"EVT-02662":{"k":"event","n":"A great fish swallows Jonah","d":"The great fish the LORD prepared swallows Jonah, who is in its belly three days and three nights (Jonah 1:17)","f":[{"p":"duration in days","r":"Jonah 1:17; Matthew 12:40","v":"3 days"},{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 1:17","e":"EVT-02658","q":4},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:17","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 1:17","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 1:17","v":"Jonah 1:17"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah"}},"EVT-02663":{"k":"event","n":"Jonah prays from the fish's belly","d":"From the fish's belly Jonah prays to the LORD his God, who brought his life up from the pit (Jonah 2:1–9)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 2:1–9","e":"EVT-02658","q":5},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 2:1","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 2:1–2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 2:1–9","v":"Jonah 2:1–9"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah"}},"EVT-02664":{"k":"event","n":"The fish vomits Jonah onto dry land","d":"At the LORD's word the fish vomits Jonah onto dry land (Jonah 2:10)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 2:10","e":"EVT-02658","q":6},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 2:10","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 2:10","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 2:10","v":"Jonah 2:10"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah"}},"EVT-02665":{"k":"event","n":"The word of the LORD comes to Jonah a second time","d":"The LORD tells Jonah again to go to Nineveh, that great city, and preach the message He gives him (Jonah 3:1–2)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Jonah 3:2","v":"Jonah was to arise and go to Nineveh, that great city, and preach to it the message the LORD would tell him"},{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 3:1–2","e":"EVT-02658","q":7},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:1","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:1–2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 3:1–2","v":"Jonah 3:1–2"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah"}},"EVT-02666":{"k":"event","n":"Jonah cries out against Nineveh","d":"Jonah goes to Nineveh as the LORD said and, on the first day's walk into the city, cries out that in forty days it will be overthrown (Jonah 3:3–4)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Jonah 3:4","v":"In forty days Nineveh would be overthrown"},{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 3:3–4","e":"EVT-02658","q":8},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:3–4","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:2–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"place","r":"Jonah 3:3–4","e":"PLC-00038"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 3:3–4","v":"Jonah 3:3–4"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah","PLC-00038":"Nineveh"}},"EVT-02667":{"k":"event","n":"The people of Nineveh repent","d":"The people of Nineveh believe God, fast and put on sackcloth, and the king and his nobles decree that man and beast fast, cry to God and turn from evil (Jonah 3:5–9)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 3:5–9","e":"EVT-02658","q":9},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:5","e":"GRP-01020"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:6–7","e":"PER-02983"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:7","e":"GRP-01021"},{"p":"place","r":"Jonah 3:5–7","e":"PLC-00038"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 3:5–9","v":"Jonah 3:5–9"}],"nm":{"EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","GRP-01020":"The people of Nineveh in Jonah's day","GRP-01021":"The nobles of the king of Nineveh in Jonah's day","PER-02983":"The king of Nineveh in Jonah's day","PLC-00038":"Nineveh"}},"EVT-02668":{"k":"event","n":"God relents from the disaster He said He would bring on Nineveh","d":"God sees that the people of Nineveh have turned from their evil way, and relents from the disaster (Jonah 3:10)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 3:10","e":"EVT-02658","q":10},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:10","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 3:10","e":"GRP-01020"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 3:10","v":"Jonah 3:10"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","GRP-01020":"The people of Nineveh in Jonah's day"}},"EVT-02669":{"k":"event","n":"Jonah is angry that the LORD spares Nineveh","d":"Jonah is greatly displeased and asks the LORD to take his life, and the LORD asks whether it is right for him to be angry (Jonah 4:1–4)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 4:1–4","e":"EVT-02658","q":11},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 4:1–3","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 4:2–4","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 4:1–4","v":"Jonah 4:1–4"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah"}},"EVT-02670":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD prepares a plant, a worm and an east wind for Jonah","d":"The LORD shades Jonah with a plant, then strikes it with a worm and sends an east wind, and asks whether He should not pity Nineveh (Jonah 4:5–11)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Jonah 4:5–11","e":"EVT-02658","q":12},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 4:5–9","e":"PER-01084"},{"p":"participant","r":"Jonah 4:6–11","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"place","r":"Jonah 4:5–8","e":"PLC-01441"},{"p":"told in","r":"Jonah 4:5–11","v":"Jonah 4:5–11"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02658":"The LORD sends Jonah to Nineveh","PER-01084":"Jonah","PLC-01441":"Jonah's shelter east of Nineveh"}},"EVT-02671":{"k":"event","n":"The prophecies of Micah","d":"The word of the LORD that came to Micah of Moresheth in the days of Jotham, Ahaz and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem (Micah 1:1)","f":[{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 1:1","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 1:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 1:1","v":"Micah 1:1"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02373","EVT-02672","EVT-02673","EVT-02674","EVT-02675","EVT-02676","EVT-02677","EVT-02678","EVT-02679","EVT-02680","EVT-02681","EVT-02682","EVT-02683","EVT-02684","EVT-02685","EVT-02686","EVT-02687","EVT-02688","EVT-02689"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02373":"Micah of Moresheth foretells that Zion will be plowed like a field","EVT-02672":"The LORD comes down against Samaria and Jerusalem","EVT-02673":"Micah's lament over the towns of Judah","EVT-02674":"The LORD's woe on those who devise iniquity","EVT-02675":"The LORD's word against those who silence His prophets","EVT-02676":"The LORD promises to gather the remnant of Israel","EVT-02677":"The LORD's word against the heads of Jacob and the prophets who make His people stray","EVT-02678":"The LORD's word of the mountain of His house in the latter days","EVT-02679":"The LORD will reign over the remnant in Mount Zion","EVT-02680":"The daughter of Zion will go to Babylon and be redeemed there","EVT-02681":"The daughter of Zion will thresh many peoples","EVT-02682":"The LORD promises a Ruler from Bethlehem Ephrathah","EVT-02683":"The LORD will deliver His people from the Assyrian","EVT-02684":"The LORD will cut off horses, strongholds, sorceries and images","EVT-02685":"The LORD's complaint against His people","EVT-02686":"The LORD's voice cries to the city","EVT-02687":"Micah's lament that the faithful man has perished","EVT-02688":"Israel's confession and the LORD's comfort","EVT-02689":"The LORD will pardon the remnant of His heritage","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02672":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD comes down against Samaria and Jerusalem","d":"The LORD comes down from His holy temple, and the mountains melt under Him, for the transgression of Jacob and the high places of Judah; He will make Samaria a heap of ruins (Micah 1:2–7)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 1:3–4","v":"The LORD would come out of His place and tread on the high places of the earth; the mountains would melt under Him and the valleys split like wax before the fire"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 1:6–7","v":"He would make Samaria a heap of ruins in the field, a place for planting a vineyard, pour her stones into the valley and uncover her foundations; her carved images would be beaten to pieces, her pay as a harlot burned and her idols laid desolate"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 1:2–7","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 1:2–7","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 1:2–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 1:2–7","v":"Micah 1:2–7"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02673":{"k":"event","n":"Micah's lament over the towns of Judah","d":"Micah wails and goes stripped and naked, for the wound has come to Judah and the gate of Jerusalem; he laments over Gath, Lachish, Mareshah, Adullam and the towns about them (Micah 1:8–16)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 1:12; Micah 1:9, 12","v":"Disaster would come down from the LORD to the gate of Jerusalem, while the inhabitant of Maroth pined (was sick, by the NKJV note) for good"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 1:16","v":"The daughter of Zion's precious children would go from her into captivity, so she was to make herself bald like an eagle"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 1:8–16","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 1:8–16","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 1:8–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 1:8–16","v":"Micah 1:8–16"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02674":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's woe on those who devise iniquity","d":"Woe to those who plan iniquity on their beds and seize the fields and houses they covet: the LORD devises disaster against this family (Micah 2:1–5)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 2:4; NKJV notes, note on Micah 2:5; Micah 2:3–5","v":"The LORD was devising disaster against this family, from which they could not remove their necks; in that day a bitter lament would be taken up over them, that their heritage (portion, by the NKJV note) was changed and their fields divided to a turncoat (an apostate, by the NKJV note), and none would cast the line (by the NKJV note) by lot in the assembly of the LORD"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 2:1–5","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 2:1–5","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 2:1–5","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 2:1–5","v":"Micah 2:1–5"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02675":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against those who silence His prophets","d":"They tell the prophets not to prattle, and rob those who pass by, yet would take a liar who prophesied of wine for their prophet (Micah 2:6–11)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 2:10","v":"They were to arise and depart, for this was not their rest; because it was defiled, it would destroy them with utter destruction"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 2:6–11","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 2:6–11","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 2:6–11","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 2:6–11","v":"Micah 2:6–11"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02676":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises to gather the remnant of Israel","d":"The LORD will gather the remnant of Israel like sheep of the fold, and the one who breaks open will go up before them, the LORD at their head (Micah 2:12–13)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 2:12; Micah 2:12","v":"He would surely assemble all of Jacob and gather the remnant of Israel, putting them together like sheep of the fold (Bozrah in Hebrew, by the NKJV note), like a flock in its pasture, loud with so many people"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 2:13","v":"The one who breaks open would come up before them; they would break out and pass through the gate, and their king would pass before them, with the LORD at their head"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 2:12–13","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 2:12–13","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 2:12–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 2:12–13","v":"Micah 2:12–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02677":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against the heads of Jacob and the prophets who make His people stray","d":"Micah charges the heads of Jacob with stripping the LORD's people and the prophets with crying peace for pay; the LORD will not answer them, but Micah is full of power by His Spirit (Micah 3:1–8)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 3:4","v":"They would cry to the LORD, but He would not hear them, and would hide His face from them at that time, because they had been evil in their deeds"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 3:6; Micah 3:6–7","v":"The prophets would have night without vision (prophetic revelation, by the NKJV note) and darkness without divination; the sun would go down on them, and the seers and diviners would be ashamed and cover their lips, for there would be no answer from God"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 3:1–8","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 3:1–8","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 3:1–8","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 3:1–8","v":"Micah 3:1–8"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02678":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word of the mountain of His house in the latter days","d":"In the latter days the mountain of the LORD's house will be exalted, the nations will learn His ways and beat their swords into plowshares (Micah 4:1–5)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Isaiah 2:2–3; Micah 4:1–2","v":"In the latter days the mountain of the LORD's house would be established on the top of the mountains and exalted above the hills, and peoples would flow to it; many nations would come to the house of the God of Jacob to be taught His ways, for the law would go forth from Zion and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem, words Isaiah also gives"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 4:3; Isaiah 2:4; Micah 4:3–4","v":"He would judge between many peoples and rebuke strong nations afar off; they would beat their swords into plowshares and their spears into pruning hooks (knives, by the NKJV note), nation would not lift up sword against nation nor learn war anymore, and everyone would sit under his vine and fig tree, unafraid, for the mouth of the LORD of hosts had spoken"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 4:1–5","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:1–5","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:1–5","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 4:1–5","v":"Micah 4:1–5"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02679":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD will reign over the remnant in Mount Zion","d":"In that day the LORD will gather the lame and the outcast, make them a strong nation and reign over them in Mount Zion forever (Micah 4:6–8)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 4:6–7","v":"In that day He would assemble the lame and gather the outcast and the afflicted, make the lame a remnant and the outcast a strong nation, and reign over them in Mount Zion from then on, forever"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 4:8","v":"The former dominion, the kingdom of the daughter of Jerusalem, would come to the tower of the flock, the stronghold of the daughter of Zion"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 4:6–8","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:6–8","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:6–8","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 4:6–8","v":"Micah 4:6–8"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02680":{"k":"event","n":"The daughter of Zion will go to Babylon and be redeemed there","d":"The daughter of Zion, in pangs like a woman in labor, will go forth from the city to Babylon, and there the LORD will redeem her (Micah 4:9–10)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 4:9; Micah 4:9–10","v":"The daughter of Zion, seized by pangs like a woman in labor (childbirth, by the NKJV note), would go forth from the city, dwell in the field and go to Babylon; there she would be delivered, and there the LORD would redeem her from the hand of her enemies"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 4:9–10","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:9–10","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:9–10","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 4:9–10","v":"Micah 4:9–10"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02681":{"k":"event","n":"The daughter of Zion will thresh many peoples","d":"The nations gathered against Zion do not know the LORD's counsel; He will gather them like sheaves, and the daughter of Zion will thresh them (Micah 4:11–13)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 4:11–13","v":"Many nations gathered against Zion, wishing to see her defiled, did not know the LORD's thoughts or counsel, for He would gather them like sheaves to the threshing floor; the daughter of Zion would arise and thresh, with horn of iron and hooves of bronze, and beat many peoples in pieces, and their gain would be consecrated to the LORD, the Lord of the whole earth"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 4:11–13","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:11–13","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 4:11–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 4:11–13","v":"Micah 4:11–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02682":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises a Ruler from Bethlehem Ephrathah","d":"Out of Bethlehem Ephrathah, little among the thousands of Judah, will come the Ruler in Israel, whose goings forth are from everlasting, and He will be peace (Micah 5:1–5)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 5:1","v":"They would lay siege against them and strike the judge of Israel with a rod on the cheek"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:2; Micah 5:2; Matthew 2:4–6; John 7:42","v":"Out of Bethlehem Ephrathah, little among the thousands of Judah, would come forth to the LORD the One to be Ruler in Israel, whose goings forth are from of old, from everlasting (the days of eternity, by the NKJV note), words the chief priests and scribes gave Herod"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:4; Micah 5:3–5","v":"He would give them up until she who is in labor had given birth; then the remnant of His brethren would return to the children of Israel, and He would stand and feed (shepherd, by the NKJV note) His flock in the strength and majesty of the name of the LORD, great to the ends of the earth, and He would be peace"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 5:1–5","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 5:1–5","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 5:1–5","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 5:1–5","v":"Micah 5:1–5"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02683":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD will deliver His people from the Assyrian","d":"When the Assyrian comes into the land, seven shepherds will waste Assyria, and the remnant of Jacob will be among the peoples like dew and like a lion (Micah 5:5–9)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:6; Micah 5:5–6","v":"When the Assyrian came into their land and trod in their palaces, they would raise against him seven shepherds and eight princely men, who would waste (devastate, by the NKJV note) the land of Assyria and the land of Nimrod at its entrances with the sword; so He would deliver them from the Assyrian"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:7; NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:9; Micah 5:7–9","v":"The remnant of Jacob would be among many peoples like dew from the LORD, like showers on the grass that wait (by the NKJV note) for no man, and among the Gentiles like a young lion among the flocks, which none can deliver from; their hand would be lifted against their adversaries, and all their enemies cut off (destroyed, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 5:5–9","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 5:5–9","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 5:5–9","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 5:5–9","v":"Micah 5:5–9"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02684":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD will cut off horses, strongholds, sorceries and images","d":"In that day the LORD will cut off Israel's horses, chariots, cities, strongholds, sorceries and images, and take vengeance on the nations (Micah 5:10–15)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:10; NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:14; Micah 5:10–14","v":"In that day He would cut off (destroy, by the NKJV note) their horses and chariots, the cities of their land and their strongholds, their sorceries and soothsayers, their carved images and sacred pillars, and pluck out their wooden images (Asherim, Canaanite deities, by the NKJV note), so that they would no more worship the work of their hands"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 5:15; Micah 5:15","v":"He would execute vengeance in anger and fury on the nations that had not heard (obeyed, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 5:10–15","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 5:10–15","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 5:10–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 5:10–15","v":"Micah 5:10–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02685":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's complaint against His people","d":"The LORD calls the mountains to hear His case against Israel, whom He brought up from Egypt, and shows what He requires: to do justly, love mercy and walk humbly with God (Micah 6:1–8)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 6:2; Micah 6:1–2","v":"The mountains and the strong foundations of the earth were to hear the LORD's complaint, for He would contend (bring charges, by the NKJV note) with Israel"},{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 6:8; Micah 6:6–8","v":"Not burnt offerings, calves a year old, thousands of rams, rivers of oil or a firstborn given for transgression, but this is what the LORD requires of man: to do justly, to love mercy (or lovingkindness, by the NKJV note) and to walk humbly with God"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 6:1–8","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 6:1–8","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 6:1–8","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 6:1–8","v":"Micah 6:1–8"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02686":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's voice cries to the city","d":"The LORD's voice cries to the city of wicked scales and violent rich men, who keep the statutes of Omri: they will eat and not be satisfied, sow and not reap (Micah 6:9–16)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 6:14; Micah 6:13–14","v":"He would strike them and make them desolate for their sins: they would eat and not be satisfied, with hunger (or emptiness or humiliation, by the NKJV note) in their midst; what they carried off they would not save, and what they rescued He would give to the sword"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 6:15","v":"They would sow and not reap, tread the olives and not anoint themselves with oil, and make sweet wine and not drink it"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 6:16; Micah 6:16","v":"He would make them a desolation (or object of horror, by the NKJV note) and their inhabitants a hissing, and they would bear the reproach of His people (of the nations, in the Septuagint, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 6:9–16","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 6:9–16","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 6:9–16","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 6:9–16","v":"Micah 6:9–16"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02687":{"k":"event","n":"Micah's lament that the faithful man has perished","d":"Micah laments that the faithful man has perished and none can trust his own household, but he will wait for the God of his salvation (Micah 7:1–7)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 7:4","v":"The day of their watchmen and of their punishment was coming, and their perplexity with it"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 7:1–7","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 7:1–7","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 7:1–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 7:1–7","v":"Micah 7:1–7"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02688":{"k":"event","n":"Israel's confession and the LORD's comfort","d":"Though fallen, Israel will rise and bear the LORD's indignation until He brings it to the light; its walls will be built and its people gathered from afar (Micah 7:8–13)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Micah 7:10","v":"The enemy who said 'Where is the LORD your God?' would see it, be covered with shame and be trampled down like mud in the streets"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 7:11; NKJV notes, note on Micah 7:12; Micah 7:11–13","v":"In the day their walls were built the decree would go far and wide (or the boundary be extended, by the NKJV note); they (the captives, by the NKJV note) would come from Assyria and the fortified cities (possibly cities of Egypt, by the NKJV note), from the fortress (possibly Egypt) to the River (the Euphrates), from sea to sea and mountain to mountain; yet the land would be desolate for the deeds of those who dwell in it"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 7:8–13","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 7:8–13","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 7:8–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 7:8–13","v":"Micah 7:8–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02689":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD will pardon the remnant of His heritage","d":"Micah asks the LORD to shepherd His flock, and the LORD will show wonders as at the Exodus; He pardons iniquity and will cast all their sins into the sea (Micah 7:14–20)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 7:15; Micah 7:15","v":"As in the days when they came out of the land of Egypt, the LORD would show them (the captives, by the NKJV note) wonders"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 7:17; Micah 7:16–17","v":"The nations would see and be ashamed of all their might, put their hands over their mouths, lick the dust like a serpent and crawl from their holes like snakes (crawlers, by the NKJV note), and fear the LORD"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Micah 7:19; NKJV notes, note on Micah 7:20; Micah 7:19–20","v":"He would again have compassion on them, subdue their iniquities and cast all their sins into the depths of the sea (the text has 'our', and the NKJV note 'Lit. their'), and give truth to Jacob and mercy (or lovingkindness, by the NKJV note) to Abraham, as He swore to their fathers from days of old"},{"p":"part of","r":"Micah 7:14–20","e":"EVT-02671"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 7:14–20","e":"PER-02870"},{"p":"participant","r":"Micah 7:14–20","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Micah 7:14–20","v":"Micah 7:14–20"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02671":"The prophecies of Micah","PER-02870":"Micah"}},"EVT-02690":{"k":"event","n":"The vision of Nahum","d":"The burden against Nineveh, the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite, in which the LORD foretells the end of Nineveh and peace for Judah (Nahum 1–3)","f":[{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:1","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:12–14","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 1–3","v":"Nahum 1–3"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02691","EVT-02692","EVT-02693","EVT-02694","EVT-02695","EVT-02696","EVT-02698"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02691":"The LORD's vengeance on His adversaries","EVT-02692":"The LORD's word against the one who plots evil against Him","EVT-02693":"The LORD promises Judah that the wicked one will pass through no more","EVT-02694":"Nahum foretells the plundering of Nineveh","EVT-02695":"The LORD of hosts is against the den of the lions","EVT-02696":"The woe on the bloody city","EVT-02698":"Nineveh will fall as No Amon fell","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02691":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's vengeance on His adversaries","d":"God is jealous and the LORD avenges; slow to anger and great in power, He is good to those who trust in Him, but with an overflowing flood He will make an utter end of its place (Nahum 1:2–8)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 1:8","v":"With an overflowing flood He would make an utter end of its place, and darkness would pursue His enemies"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 1:2–8","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:2–8","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:2–8","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 1:2–8","v":"Nahum 1:2–8"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02692":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against the one who plots evil against Him","d":"What is plotted against the LORD He will bring to an utter end, and the plotters will be devoured like dry stubble; the one from whom a wicked counselor has come is to have no name and no images left, and the LORD will dig its grave (Nahum 1:9–11, 14)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 1:9; Nahum 1:9–10","v":"Whatever they conspired (or devised, by the NKJV note) against the LORD, He would bring to an utter end, and affliction would not rise up a second time; tangled like thorns and drunk like drunkards, they would be devoured like stubble fully dried"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 1:14; Nahum 1:14","v":"The LORD commanded concerning the one addressed that its name be perpetuated no longer (lit. that no more of it be fruitful, by the NKJV note), that the carved image and the molded image be cut off from the house of its gods, and that He dig its grave, for it was vile (or contemptible, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 1:9–11, 14","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:9–11, 14","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:14","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 1:9–11, 14","v":"Nahum 1:9–11, 14"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02693":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises Judah that the wicked one will pass through no more","d":"The LORD will afflict no more the one He afflicted, but break off the oppressor's yoke; on the mountains come the feet of him who brings good tidings, and Judah is to keep its feasts and vows (Nahum 1:12–13, 15)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Nahum 1:15","v":"With the feet of him who brings good tidings and proclaims peace on the mountains, Judah was to keep its appointed feasts and perform its vows"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 1:12; Nahum 1:12–13","v":"Though they were safe (or at peace or complete, by the NKJV note) and many, they would be cut down when he passed through; and the LORD, who had afflicted the one He spoke to, would afflict no more, but break off his yoke and burst the bonds apart"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 1:15; Nahum 1:15","v":"The wicked one (one of Belial, lit., by the NKJV note) would no more pass through Judah, for he is utterly cut off"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 1:12–13, 15","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:12–13, 15","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 1:12","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 1:12–13, 15","v":"Nahum 1:12–13, 15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02694":{"k":"event","n":"Nahum foretells the plundering of Nineveh","d":"He who scatters comes up against Nineveh: his chariots rage in the streets, the gates of the rivers are opened, she is led away captive, her people flee and her silver and gold are taken as spoil (Nahum 2:1–10)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 2:1; Nahum 2:1","v":"He who scatters (He who destroys, in the Vulgate, by the NKJV note) had come up before her face, though she might man the fort, watch the road, strengthen her flanks and fortify her power"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 2:2","v":"The LORD would restore the excellence of Jacob like the excellence of Israel, for the emptiers had emptied them out and ruined their vine branches"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 2:3; Nahum 2:3–4","v":"The shields of his mighty men would be red and his valiant men in scarlet; his chariots would come with flaming torches in the day of his preparation, the spears brandished (lit. the cypresses shaken, by the NKJV note), raging in the streets, jostling in the broad roads and running like lightning"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 2:5–6","v":"He would remember his nobles, who would stumble in their haste to her walls to prepare the defense; the gates of the rivers would be opened and the palace dissolved"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 2:7; Nahum 2:7","v":"It was decreed (Huzzab in Hebrew, by the NKJV note) that she be led away captive, her maidservants leading her with the voice of doves and beating their breasts"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 2:8–10","v":"Nineveh's people would flee, none turning back though they cried 'Halt!'; her silver and gold would be taken as spoil, with no end of treasure, and she would be empty, desolate and waste, hearts melting and knees shaking"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 2:1–10","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 2:1–10","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 2:2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 2:1–10","v":"Nahum 2:1–10"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02695":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD of hosts is against the den of the lions","d":"Where now is the den of the lions, where the lion filled his caves with prey? The LORD of hosts is against it, and the voice of its messengers will be heard no more (Nahum 2:11–13)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 2:13","v":"The LORD of hosts was against it: He would burn the chariots in smoke, the sword would devour the young lions, He would cut off the prey from the earth, and the voice of the messengers would be heard no more"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 2:11–13","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 2:11–13","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 2:13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 2:11–13","v":"Nahum 2:11–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02696":{"k":"event","n":"The woe on the bloody city","d":"Woe to the bloody city, full of lies and robbery, the harlot and mistress of sorceries who sells nations: the LORD of hosts is against her, and all who see her will say that Nineveh is laid waste (Nahum 3:1–7)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 3:2; Nahum 3:2–3","v":"The noise of the whip and the rattling wheels, of galloping horses and clattering (bounding or jolting, by the NKJV note) chariots, would fill her, with horsemen charging with bright sword and glittering spear, a multitude of slain and corpses beyond counting, over which they stumble"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Nahum 3:6; Nahum 3:5–7","v":"The LORD of hosts was against her: He would lift her skirts over her face and show the nations her nakedness and the kingdoms her shame, cast abominable filth on her and make her vile (despicable, by the NKJV note) and a spectacle; all who looked on her would flee from her and say that Nineveh was laid waste, with none to bemoan her"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 3:1–7","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 3:1–7","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 3:5–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 3:1–7","v":"Nahum 3:1–7"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02697":{"k":"event","n":"No Amon is carried away into captivity","d":"No Amon, by the River with the waters around her and the sea for her wall, whose strength was Ethiopia and Egypt, was carried away into captivity: her young children were dashed to pieces at the head of every street, lots were cast for her honorable men and all her great men were bound in chains (Nahum 3:8–10)","f":[{"p":"occurred before","r":"Nahum 3:8–10","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"place","r":"Nahum 3:8–10","e":"PLC-01329"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 3:8–10","v":"Nahum 3:8–10"}],"nm":{"EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PLC-01329":"No"}},"EVT-02698":{"k":"event","n":"Nineveh will fall as No Amon fell","d":"Nineveh is no better than No Amon, which went into captivity: her strongholds will fall like ripe figs, fire and sword will devour her, and the shepherds of the king of Assyria slumber, his wound without healing (Nahum 3:8–19)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 3:11–13","v":"Nineveh too would be drunk and hidden and seek refuge from the enemy; her strongholds would be like fig trees with ripe figs that fall into the eater's mouth when shaken; her people would be as women in her midst, the gates of her land wide open to her enemies and fire devouring their bars"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 3:14–17","v":"Though she drew water for the siege, strengthened her forts and trod the clay for her brick kilns, fire would devour her and the sword cut her off, eating her up like the locust; her merchants, multiplied beyond the stars of heaven, and her commanders and generals would be like locusts camped in the hedges on a cold day, which fly away when the sun rises and are not found"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Nahum 3:18–19","v":"The shepherds of the king of Assyria would slumber and his nobles rest in the dust, his people scattered on the mountains with none to gather them; his wound would have no healing, and all who heard the news would clap their hands over him"},{"p":"part of","r":"Nahum 3:8–19","e":"EVT-02690"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 3:8–19","e":"PER-02984"},{"p":"participant","r":"Nahum 3:5–8","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Nahum 3:8–19","v":"Nahum 3:8–19"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02690":"The vision of Nahum","PER-02984":"Nahum"}},"EVT-02699":{"k":"event","n":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","d":"The burden which the prophet Habakkuk saw, his complaints to the LORD and the LORD's answers, and his prayer on Shigionoth (Habakkuk 1–3)","f":[{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:1","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:5; 2:2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 1–3","v":"Habakkuk 1–3"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02700","EVT-02701","EVT-02702","EVT-02703","EVT-02704","EVT-02705"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02700":"Habakkuk cries to the LORD against violence","EVT-02701":"The LORD answers that He is raising up the Chaldeans","EVT-02702":"Habakkuk asks why the LORD looks on the treacherous","EVT-02703":"The LORD bids Habakkuk write the vision","EVT-02704":"The LORD's woes on the proud man who gathers the nations","EVT-02705":"Habakkuk prays that the LORD revive His work","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02700":{"k":"event","n":"Habakkuk cries to the LORD against violence","d":"Habakkuk asks the LORD how long he must cry out against violence and not be heard, for the law is powerless and justice perverted (Habakkuk 1:2–4)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Habakkuk 1:2–4","e":"EVT-02699","q":1},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:2–4","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:2–4","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 1:2–4","v":"Habakkuk 1:2–4"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02699":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02701":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD answers that He is raising up the Chaldeans","d":"The LORD will work a work in their days they would not believe: He is raising up the Chaldeans, a bitter and hasty nation that comes for violence and gathers captives like sand (Habakkuk 1:5–11)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Habakkuk 1:5; Acts 13:14–16, 40–41","v":"He would work a work in their days that they would not believe though it were told them, so that, looking among the nations, they would be utterly astounded; Paul gave these words as a warning in Antioch in Pisidia"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Habakkuk 1:6","v":"He was raising up the Chaldeans, a bitter and hasty nation, to march through the breadth of the earth and possess dwelling places not their own"},{"p":"part of","r":"Habakkuk 1:5–11","e":"EVT-02699","q":2},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:5–11","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:5–11","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 1:5–11","v":"Habakkuk 1:5–11"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02699":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02702":{"k":"event","n":"Habakkuk asks why the LORD looks on the treacherous","d":"Habakkuk owns the LORD as from everlasting and asks why He, of purer eyes than to behold evil, looks on the treacherous who catch men like fish; he stands his watch to hear His answer (Habakkuk 1:12–2:1)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Habakkuk 1:12–2:1","e":"EVT-02699","q":3},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:12–2:1","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 1:12–2:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 1:12–2:1","v":"Habakkuk 1:12–2:1"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02699":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02703":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD bids Habakkuk write the vision","d":"The LORD answers Habakkuk: he is to write the vision plainly on tablets, for it will surely come at its appointed time; the just will live by his faith (Habakkuk 2:2–4)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Habakkuk 2:2","v":"Habakkuk was to write the vision and make it plain on tablets, that he who reads it may run"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Habakkuk 2:3; Hebrews 10:37","v":"The vision was for an appointed time; at the end it would speak and not lie, and though it tarried it was to be waited for, for it would surely come and not tarry, words taken up in Hebrews 10:37"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Habakkuk 2:4; Romans 1:17; Galatians 3:11; Hebrews 10:38","v":"The proud man's soul is not upright in him, but the just man will live by his faith, words taken up in Romans 1:17, Galatians 3:11 and Hebrews 10:38"},{"p":"part of","r":"Habakkuk 2:2–4","e":"EVT-02699","q":4},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 2:2–4","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 2:2–4","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 2:2–4","v":"Habakkuk 2:2–4"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02699":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02704":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's woes on the proud man who gathers the nations","d":"The nations will take up a taunt against the proud man who gathers them to himself: woe to the plunderer, to him who covets evil gain, who builds a town with bloodshed, who makes his neighbor drunk and who trusts in mute idols; but the LORD is in His holy temple (Habakkuk 2:5–20)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Habakkuk 2:20","v":"All the earth was to keep silence before the LORD, who is in His holy temple"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:6; NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:7; NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:8; Habakkuk 2:6–8","v":"All the nations would take up a taunt against him: woe to him who increases what is not his and loads himself with many pledges (thick clay, in the Syriac and the Vulgate, by the NKJV note); his creditors (lit. those who bite him, by the NKJV note) would rise up suddenly and make him their booty, and because he plundered many nations, the remnant of the peoples would plunder him, for men's blood (or bloodshed, by the NKJV note) and the violence done to the land and the city"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:9; Habakkuk 2:9–11","v":"Woe to him who covets evil gain for his house, to set his nest on high and escape the power (lit. hand, by the NKJV note) of disaster: he has given his house shameful counsel, cutting off many peoples and sinning against his own soul, and the stone will cry out from the wall and the beam answer it from the timbers"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:13; Habakkuk 2:12–14","v":"Woe to him who builds a town with bloodshed and establishes a city by iniquity: it is of the LORD of hosts that the peoples labor to feed the fire (lit. for what satisfies fire, for what is of no lasting value, by the NKJV note) and the nations weary themselves in vain, for the earth will be filled with the knowledge of the LORD's glory as the waters cover the sea"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:15; NKJV notes, note on Habakkuk 2:16; Habakkuk 2:15–17","v":"Woe to him who gives his neighbor drink, pressing (lit. attaching or joining, by the NKJV note) him to the bottle to look on his nakedness: he would be filled with shame instead of glory, drink and be exposed as uncircumcised (reel, in the Dead Sea Scrolls and the Septuagint, by the NKJV note), the cup of the LORD's right hand would be turned against him, and the violence done to Lebanon and the plunder of beasts would cover him"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Habakkuk 2:18–19","v":"Woe to him who bids wood awake and silent stone arise: the carved and molded image is a teacher of lies, of no profit to the maker who trusts in it, overlaid with gold and silver but with no breath in it"},{"p":"part of","r":"Habakkuk 2:5–20","e":"EVT-02699","q":5},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 2:5–20","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 2:2, 13, 20","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 2:5–20","v":"Habakkuk 2:5–20"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02699":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02705":{"k":"event","n":"Habakkuk prays that the LORD revive His work","d":"Habakkuk, afraid at the LORD's speech, prays Him to revive His work and in wrath remember mercy; he recalls God's coming from Teman and His salvation, and will rejoice in the God of his salvation though all fails (Habakkuk 3:1–19)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Habakkuk 3:1","e":"EVT-02699"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 3:1–2","e":"PER-02985"},{"p":"participant","r":"Habakkuk 3:2","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Habakkuk 3:1–19","v":"Habakkuk 3:1–19"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02699":"The prophecies of Habakkuk","PER-02985":"Habakkuk"}},"EVT-02706":{"k":"event","n":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","d":"The word of the LORD that came to Zephaniah in the days of Josiah son of Amon, king of Judah (Zephaniah 1:1)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 1:1","e":"EVT-01858"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:1","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:1","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 1:1","v":"Zephaniah 1:1"}],"rv":{"inc":["EVT-02707","EVT-02708","EVT-02709","EVT-02710","EVT-02711","EVT-02712","EVT-02713","EVT-02714","EVT-02715","EVT-02716","EVT-02717"]},"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-01858":"The reign of Josiah","EVT-02707":"The LORD will consume all from the face of the land","EVT-02708":"The LORD stretches out His hand against Judah and Jerusalem","EVT-02709":"The day of the LORD's sacrifice against Jerusalem","EVT-02710":"The great day of the LORD is near","EVT-02711":"Zephaniah calls the meek to seek the LORD before His day","EVT-02712":"The LORD's word against the Philistines","EVT-02713":"The LORD's word against Moab and Ammon","EVT-02714":"The LORD's word against the Ethiopians and Assyria","EVT-02715":"The LORD's woe on the oppressing city","EVT-02716":"The LORD promises a pure language and a humble remnant","EVT-02717":"The LORD rejoices over Zion with singing","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02707":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD will consume all from the face of the land","d":"The LORD will utterly consume everything from the face of the land, man and beast, birds and fish, and the stumbling blocks with the wicked (Zephaniah 1:2–3)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 1:2; NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 1:3; Zephaniah 1:2–3","v":"He would utterly consume (lit. make a complete end of, by the NKJV note) everything from the face of the land: man and beast, the birds of the heavens and the fish of the sea, and the stumbling blocks (idols, by the NKJV note) with the wicked, cutting off man from the face of the land (ground, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 1:2–3","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:2–3","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:2–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 1:2–3","v":"Zephaniah 1:2–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02708":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD stretches out His hand against Judah and Jerusalem","d":"The LORD will cut off every trace of Baal from Jerusalem, the idolatrous priests, those who worship the host of heaven or swear by Milcom, and those who have turned back from Him (Zephaniah 1:4–6)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 1:4; NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 1:5; Zephaniah 1:4–6","v":"He would stretch out His hand against Judah and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and cut off from this place every trace of Baal, the names of the idolatrous priests (chemarim in Hebrew, by the NKJV note) with the pagan priests, those who worship the host of heaven on the housetops, those who swear by Milcom (or Malcam, an Ammonite god, by the NKJV note), and those who have turned back from following the LORD"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 1:4–6","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:4–6","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:4–6","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 1:4–6","v":"Zephaniah 1:4–6"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02709":{"k":"event","n":"The day of the LORD's sacrifice against Jerusalem","d":"All are to be silent before the Lord GOD: on the day of His sacrifice He will punish the princes and the king's children, search Jerusalem with lamps and make its goods booty and its houses a desolation (Zephaniah 1:7–13)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 1:7; Zephaniah 1:7","v":"All were to be silent in the presence of the Lord GOD, for the day of the LORD was at hand: the LORD had prepared a sacrifice and invited (lit. set apart, consecrated, by the NKJV note) His guests"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 1:8–9","v":"In the day of the LORD's sacrifice He would punish the princes, the king's children and all who are clothed with foreign apparel, and all who leap over the threshold and fill their masters' houses with violence and deceit"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 1:11; Zephaniah 1:10–11","v":"There would be a mournful cry from the Fish Gate, a wailing from the Second Quarter and a loud crashing from the hills; the inhabitants of Maktesh (a market district of Jerusalem, lit. Mortar, by the NKJV note) would wail, for the merchant people would be cut down and all who handle money cut off"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 1:12–13","v":"He would search Jerusalem with lamps and punish those men; their goods would become booty and their houses a desolation, and they would build houses and not live in them, plant vineyards and not drink their wine"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 1:7–13","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:7–13","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:7–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 1:7–13","v":"Zephaniah 1:7–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02710":{"k":"event","n":"The great day of the LORD is near","d":"The great day of the LORD is near and hastens: a day of wrath, trouble, darkness and alarm against the fortified cities, when neither silver nor gold will deliver, and the whole land is devoured by the fire of His jealousy (Zephaniah 1:14–18)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 1:14–16","v":"The great day of the LORD was near and hastening, its noise bitter, with the mighty men crying out: a day of wrath, trouble and distress, devastation and desolation, darkness and gloominess, clouds and thick darkness, trumpet and alarm against the fortified cities and the high towers"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 1:17–18","v":"He would bring distress on men, who would walk like the blind because they sinned against the LORD, their blood poured out like dust and their flesh like refuse; neither silver nor gold would deliver them, and the whole land would be devoured by the fire of His jealousy, for He would make speedy riddance of all who dwell in it"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 1:14–18","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:14–18","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 1:14–18","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 1:14–18","v":"Zephaniah 1:14–18"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02711":{"k":"event","n":"Zephaniah calls the meek to seek the LORD before His day","d":"The nation is to gather before the decree is issued, and the meek of the earth are to seek the LORD, righteousness and humility, that they may be hidden in the day of His anger (Zephaniah 2:1–3)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 2:1; Zephaniah 2:1–2","v":"The undesirable (or shameless, by the NKJV note) nation was to gather together before the decree was issued and the day passed like chaff, before the day of the LORD's fierce anger came upon them"},{"p":"commandment","r":"Zephaniah 2:3","v":"All the meek of the earth who had upheld His justice were to seek the LORD, righteousness and humility, that they might perhaps be hidden in the day of the LORD's anger"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 2:1–3","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:1–3","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:1–3","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 2:1–3","v":"Zephaniah 2:1–3"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02712":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against the Philistines","d":"Gaza will be forsaken, Ashkelon desolate, Ashdod driven out and Ekron uprooted; the LORD is against Canaan, land of the Philistines, and its coast will be for the remnant of Judah (Zephaniah 2:4–7)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 2:4","v":"Gaza would be forsaken and Ashkelon desolate; Ashdod would be driven out at noonday and Ekron uprooted"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 2:6; Zephaniah 2:5–6","v":"Woe to the inhabitants of the seacoast, the nation of the Cherethites: the LORD would destroy Canaan, land of the Philistines, till no inhabitant was left, and the seacoast would be pastures, with shelters (underground huts or cisterns, lit. excavations, by the NKJV note) for shepherds and folds for flocks"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 2:7; Zephaniah 2:7","v":"The coast would be for the remnant of the house of Judah, who would feed their flocks there and lie down at evening in the houses of Ashkelon, for the LORD their God would intervene for them (lit. visit them, by the NKJV note) and return their captives"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 2:4–7","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:4–7","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:4–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 2:4–7","v":"Zephaniah 2:4–7"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02713":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against Moab and Ammon","d":"For their reproach against His people, Moab will be like Sodom and the people of Ammon like Gomorrah, and the LORD will reduce the gods of the earth to nothing (Zephaniah 2:8–11)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 2:9; Zephaniah 2:9","v":"The LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, swore by His life that Moab would be like Sodom and the people of Ammon like Gomorrah, overrun with weeds (lit. possessed by nettles, by the NKJV note) and saltpits, a perpetual desolation (or permanent ruin), and that the residue and remnant of His people would plunder and possess them"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 2:11","v":"The LORD would be awesome to them, reducing all the gods of the earth to nothing, and all the shores of the nations would worship Him, each from his place"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 2:8–11","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:8–11","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:8–11","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 2:8–11","v":"Zephaniah 2:8–11"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02714":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's word against the Ethiopians and Assyria","d":"The Ethiopians will be slain by His sword, and He will destroy Assyria and make Nineveh, the rejoicing city, a desolation as dry as the wilderness (Zephaniah 2:12–15)","f":[{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 2:12","v":"The Ethiopians would be slain by His sword"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 2:13–15","v":"He would stretch out His hand against the north, destroy Assyria and make Nineveh a desolation as dry as the wilderness: herds and every beast would lie down in her midst, the pelican and the bittern would lodge on the capitals of her pillars and sing in her windows, desolation would sit at the threshold and her cedar work be laid bare, and all who passed by would hiss and shake their fists"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 2:12–15","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:12–15","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 2:12–15","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 2:12–15","v":"Zephaniah 2:12–15"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02715":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD's woe on the oppressing city","d":"Woe to the rebellious, polluted and oppressing city, whose princes, judges, prophets and priests have done evil, though the LORD is righteous in her midst and cut off nations as a warning to her (Zephaniah 3:1–7)","f":[{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 3:1–7","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 3:1–7","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 3:5–7","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 3:1–7","v":"Zephaniah 3:1–7"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02716":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD promises a pure language and a humble remnant","d":"They are to wait for the day He rises up: He will gather the nations for His indignation, give the peoples a pure language to call on His name, and leave a meek and humble remnant of Israel (Zephaniah 3:8–13)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 3:8; Zephaniah 3:8","v":"They were to wait for the LORD until the day He rose up for plunder (for witness, in the Septuagint and the Syriac, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 3:8","v":"He was determined to gather the nations and the kingdoms to pour on them His indignation and all His fierce anger, and all the earth would be devoured with the fire of His jealousy"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 3:9; Zephaniah 3:9–10","v":"He would restore to the peoples a pure language (lit. lip, by the NKJV note), that all might call on the name of the LORD and serve Him with one accord; from beyond the rivers of Ethiopia His worshipers, the daughter of His dispersed ones, would bring His offering"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 3:11–13","v":"He would take away from her midst those who rejoice in pride and leave a meek and humble people who trust in His name; the remnant of Israel would do no unrighteousness and speak no lies, and would feed their flocks and lie down with none to make them afraid"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 3:8–13","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 3:8–13","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 3:8–13","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 3:8–13","v":"Zephaniah 3:8–13"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}},"EVT-02717":{"k":"event","n":"The LORD rejoices over Zion with singing","d":"The daughter of Zion is to sing, for the LORD, the King of Israel, is in her midst: He will rejoice over her with singing, gather the outcasts and return her captives before her eyes (Zephaniah 3:14–20)","f":[{"p":"commandment","r":"Zephaniah 3:14","v":"The daughter of Zion was to sing, Israel to shout, and the daughter of Jerusalem to be glad and rejoice with all her heart"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 3:15; Zephaniah 3:15–16","v":"The LORD had taken away her judgments and cast out her enemy; the King of Israel, the LORD, was in her midst, and she would see (fear, in the Masoretic text and the Vulgate, by the NKJV note) disaster no more; Jerusalem would be told not to fear, nor Zion to let her hands be weak"},{"p":"foretold","r":"Zephaniah 3:17","v":"The LORD her God in her midst, the Mighty One, would save; He would rejoice over her with gladness, quiet her with His love and rejoice over her with singing"},{"p":"foretold","r":"NKJV notes, note on Zephaniah 3:20; Zephaniah 3:18–20","v":"He would gather those who sorrow over the appointed assembly, deal with all who afflict her, save the lame and gather those driven out, and give them fame and praise (lit. a name, by the NKJV note) among all the peoples when He returned their captives before their eyes"},{"p":"part of","r":"Zephaniah 3:14–20","e":"EVT-02706"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 3:14–20","e":"PER-02986"},{"p":"participant","r":"Zephaniah 3:14–20","e":"DEI-00001"},{"p":"told in","r":"Zephaniah 3:14–20","v":"Zephaniah 3:14–20"}],"nm":{"DEI-00001":"God","EVT-02706":"The prophecies of Zephaniah","PER-02986":"Zephaniah"}}});
